window.receiveProjectSource({"path": ".docs/specs/people_entities.md", "lines": ["# SPEC \u2014 People as platform entities (PVW)", "", "| | |", "|---|---|", "| **Status** | Decisions D1\u2013D14 all ratified. Three rounds of external PRD review triaged and applied (2026-08-20, 2026-08-25, 2026-08-26): D4, D8 and D13 amended in place; T4 and T9 merged; twelve claims re-verified against source (Appendix A). Round 3 reports the architecture stable. Filing follows as **one epic plus eight stories, T1\u2013T8**. T0 is closed evidence and is not filed; T9 was merged into T4 and does not exist. |", "| **Date** | 2026-08-18; last revised 2026-08-26 |", "| **Owner** | CTO (registry/type decisions); DataLake2 + Accelerate platform for implementation |", "| **Program** | Entity registry expansion \u2014 people facet |", "| **Repos** | DataLake2, Accelerate (`accelerate_models` + platform) |", "| **Related** | Entity Registry Expansion epic DAT-7349 (org facet, shipped), `accelerate/.docs/prds/signal-engine-v1.9.md` \u00a73.4, `.docs/codebase/ENTITY_MATCHING.md`, `.docs/codebase/CANDIDATE_ROLLUP_CONTRACT.md` |", "", "---", "", "## 0. The answer, up front", "", "**What this buys.** Two capabilities the platform does not have today:", "", "1. **Users can point an intelligence agent at a person.** Watch a CEO, a founder, a", "   regulator, a portfolio-company operator the way an agent watches a company today \u2014 and", "   get the events that person is actually the subject of, not the events their employer", "   happened to be named in.", "2. **The entity relationship picture gets its missing dimension.** The registry already", "   models legal hierarchy (company owns company) and brand operation (brand run by", "   company). People are the third kind of edge that makes an intelligence graph", "   worth querying: who leads what, who they left to get there, who sits on which board. None of that", "   is expressible while people are not entities.", "", "**Why it does not work today.** Extraction finds people and matching resolves them against", "master data \u2014 and then the person is dropped. Person matches are never stamped with", "`platform_entity_id`, and every unstamped row is filtered out before the event-extraction", "prompt is built. A story about a person carries the person's *employer*, never the person.", "", "What this spec proposes:", "", "1. **Add `PVW` (PersonView) as a platform entity type**, backed by a new `pvw.persons`", "   table, following the exact pattern `BVW` / `BRV` already shipped with. All downstream", "   plumbing (`source_event_entities`, `signal_entities`, closure, merge) is already", "   entity-type-agnostic; the registry row is the only missing link.", "2. **Identity is ours, not a vendor's.** A person gets a Polaris person row and a canonical", "   platform UUID. Every external id \u2014 The Official Board, Prospeo, whatever comes next \u2014 is a", "   *resolution key* in a source-id table, so a vendor change never re-keys the registry and two", "   vendors' ids for one human resolve to one person.", "3. **Four lifecycle states, so real people are not stuck outside.** Verified sources admit officers", "   directly. Unanchored people \u2014 the actor, the athlete, the founder, the politician \u2014 are minted", "   provisionally once they clear an evidence bar, and are promoted by review. Everyone else stays an", "   observation and accumulates evidence. Only `VERIFIED`, `PROVISIONAL` and `EVIDENCE_PROMOTED` have", "   canonical person rows; `OBSERVED` stays in the candidate store.", "4. **Name-based dedup is explicitly rejected for people.** The business rollup dedupes on", "   normalized name; for people that would merge every John Smith in the corpus. The person", "   rollup groups on `(normalized_name, anchor)` and is a review surface, not an identity.", "5. **Nothing about existing attribution changes.** `doc.doc_entity_map` stays `corp_id`-keyed and", "   `Person: {name}` reasons keep pointing at the employer's corp. All new work sits beside the", "   trunk.", "6. **Person\u2194company affiliation ships as a typed edge**, in the same store that already holds", "   legal hierarchy and brand operation \u2014 and it is excluded from the ownership-closure walk, so a", "   person's event never silently becomes their employer's event (D6).", "", "Every decision in \u00a74 is **ratified** (\u00a74, D1\u2013D14). The measurement that gated the seed design is", "**done** \u2014 \u00a77 carries the numbers. Two follow-up queries remain and are named there (\u00a77.3, \u00a77.6);", "neither blocks filing.", "", "---", "", "## 1. The capability gap", "", "### 1.1 What an agent can and cannot watch", "", "An agent today can scope to a company, a market, or an industry. It cannot scope to a person,", "because no person has a canonical entity id to scope *to*. The consequence chain below is", "schema-level, not a tuning problem \u2014 there is no configuration that makes a person watchable.", "", "### 1.2 The consequence chain (verified against source, 2026-08-18)", "", "| Step | What happens | Source |", "|---|---|---|", "| 1 | LLM extracts people with names, `is_owner`, evidence, confidence | `entity_classification/services/helpers/people_funcs.py` |", "| 2 | Names match `nvw_match.master_text` \u2192 `text_match_xref` \u2192 `nvw_match.entities` rows whose `context.type = 'person'` | `.docs/codebase/ENTITY_MATCHING.md` |", "| 3 | A `matched_entities` row is written with `platform_entity_id=None` \u2014 **always**, by design | `people_funcs.py:93-106` (\"Person rows are NEVER stamped \u2026 Stamping happens only on the org call-site\") |", "| 4 | `build_known_entity_refs` drops every person match, then drops every remaining row with a NULL `platform_entity_id`, **before the prompt is built** | `event_extraction/services/helpers/prompt_context.py:86-108` |", "| 5 | So no person appears in `raw_events.entities_involved` | `event_extraction/services/extraction_service.py:480-484` (the provenance-key map admits `CVW`/`MVW`/`IVW` only) |", "| 6 | So no person appears in `event_synth.source_event_entities`, and no agent can watch one | `event_synthesis/services/entity_display_names.py:90` (hard allowlist `{CVW, MVW, IVW}`) |", "", "The person is not lost inside DataLake2 \u2014 `entity_classification.people` rows persist with", "name parts, `is_owner`, evidence and confidence, matched or not. The person never leaves", "DataLake2.", "", "### 1.3 What a person mention does instead", "", "A matched person resolves to the `corp_id` of the company they are an officer or CEO of, and", "produces a CVW attribution labelled `Entity CEO: {name}`, `Subsidiary CEO: {name}`, or", "`Person: {name}` (`nvw_match.categories.priority` 25 / 45 / 999). \"Jeff Bezos\" attributes the", "article to Amazon. There is no Bezos entity, and an agent cannot watch Bezos.", "", "### 1.4 Who is missing entirely", "", "The master-data person population is officer- and board-derived: the person provenance tables", "are `off_brd.id_match` (officer/board id \u2192 company corp_id) and `refinitiv.ceos` (CEO \u2192 the", "company they lead), and `nvw_match.entities_context` carries `job_title` and `ob_exec_id`.", "A person with no corporate officer role has no master record, so they never match. For those", "people the pipeline produces an `entity_classification.people` row with `matched_entity_id =", "NULL` and nothing else \u2014 no candidate row (the candidate store is organizations-only), no", "aggregation across articles, no downstream trace.", "", "That is the whole population behind stories like a celebrity death or a criminal proceeding:", "the subject of the story is structurally unrepresentable.", "", "---", "", "## 2. Current state \u2014 what changed since the last write-up", "", "The org facet of this problem (Entity Registry Expansion, DAT-7349) has largely", "shipped, which makes the people work far cheaper than the epic assumed. Verified against", "`accelerate_models` and a local `accelerate` database, 2026-08-18:", "", "| Capability | State | Evidence |", "|---|---|---|", "| `ent.entities` typed-FK registry | **Shipped**, five bridged types | `common/models/entities.py` \u2014 `corp_id`, `market_id`, `industry_id`, `business_id`, `brand_id`; `entities_typed_fk_chk` |", "| `AccountType` enum | **Six values**: `CVW`, `MVW`, `GVW`, `IVW`, `BVW`, `BRV` | `common/models/enum/account_type.py`; `select enum_range(NULL::acc.account_type)` |", "| Live rows by type (local dev) | CVW 1710 \u00b7 MVW 120 \u00b7 IVW 66 \u00b7 BVW 32 \u00b7 BRV 32 | `select entity_type, count(*) from ent.entities group by 1` |", "| Backing tables for new types | **Thin stubs**: `bvw.businesses`, `brv.brands` = `(id, name UNIQUE)`, ids minted externally | `accounts/app/models/{business_view/businesses,brand_view/brands}.py` |", "| Relationship-edge store | **Shipped** \u2014 `ent.entity_relationships`, families `LEGAL_HIERARCHY` / `BRAND_OPERATION` / `ASSOCIATIVE` | `common/models/entity_relationships.py` |", "| Merge / supersede | **Shipped** \u2014 `ent.entities.superseded_by`, `ent.entity_merge_history`, `MergeReason` = `GRADUATION` / `DEDUP` / `PROMOTION` / `ACCOUNT_GRADUATION` | `common/models/entity_merge_history.py` |", "| Ownership closure | **Shipped** DataLake2-side | `event_synthesis/services/ownership_closure.py` |", "| Candidate observation store | **Shipped, organizations only** | `entity_classification/models/candidate_observations.py`; `.docs/codebase/CANDIDATE_ROLLUP_CONTRACT.md` |", "| Context capture on extracted entities | **Shipped for organizations** (`organizations.context` JSONB); **absent for people** | `entity_classification/models/{organizations,people}.py` |", "| `GVW` | Enum value with **no** bridge \u2014 no `gvw` schema, no typed FK column | `entities.py` CHECK constraint; local `pg_namespace` |", "", "Two consequences for this spec:", "", "- **PVW is no longer a first-of-kind extension.** There is a working two-instance precedent", "  (BVW, BRV) for the enum value, typed FK, CHECK, partial-unique index, trigger and backfill.", "- **`GVW` shows the failure mode to avoid.** An `AccountType` value without a registry bridge", "  is silently dropped at ESS with `invalid_entity_skipped reason=entity_type_not_bridged`.", "  The enum value and the bridge must land in the same change.", "", "### 2.1 Stale premises in prior documents", "", "These are corrected here so no one re-derives from them. Full list in Appendix B.", "", "| Claim (where) | Correction |", "|---|---|", "| \"`AccountType` admits CVW/MVW/IVW \u2014 nothing else\" (people handoff, fact 1) | Six values today, five bridged into `ent.entities` |", "| \"no X-VW extension has been implemented yet, so this epic's keystone is the first\" (org EPIC \u00a74A) | BVW and BRV shipped; PVW follows a proven pattern |", "| \"PERSON entities \u2026 People are referenced via XVW today through `data_source_id`, which is not a stable canonical key \u2026 will introduce a canonical person table and an `xvw_id` (or equivalent) FK\" (PRD \u00a73.4) | The mechanism is right; the source population is wrong. `xvw` is client-scoped contact data, not a news-subject person master (D9) |", "| \"there is no `superseded_by` / merge history\" (PRD \u00a73.4) | Shipped |", "| \"It is `kads.people_cards`, not `xvw.people_cards`\" (people handoff, fact 7) | Both name the same table. The code module is `accelerate_models/kads/`; the physical schema is `xvw` (`KADS_SCHEMA=xvw` in `accelerate/.env` and `.env.template`) |", "| `ob_exec_id` documented as \"Execution or run identifier\" (`entity_classification/schemas/industry_references.py:66`) | It is the officer/board provider's **executive person id** \u2014 see D1 |", "| ESS docstring \"`ent.entities` only bridges CVW/MVW/IVW per the `entities_typed_fk_chk` check constraint\" (`entity_display_names.py:36`) | Stale: BVW and BRV are bridged. The allowlist drops them today, latent because nothing emits them (\u00a78, T4) |", "", "---", "", "## 3. Goals and non-goals", "", "### Goals", "", "- **Agents can watch people.** A person becomes a real `ent.entities` row that can appear in", "  an agent's `primary_entities[]` / `secondary_entities[]` scope and in `signal_entities`", "  routing, on the same footing as a company.", "- **Events link to the people they are about.** A person reaches", "  `raw_events.entities_involved` and `source_event_entities` with a role, so the event record", "  says who it concerns.", "- **The relationship picture gains people.** Person\u2194company affiliation is expressible as a", "  typed edge in the same store that already holds legal hierarchy and brand operation, so the", "  graph can answer who leads what, and who a person's previous affiliation was.", "- **The data behind a corp-hub people view exists and is queryable.** After T5 a reverse lookup on", "  the affiliation edge returns the officers and executives we hold for a corporation, each resolvable", "  to their events through their own entity id. **This epic ships the data and the query, not the", "  surface.** No story builds a hub view, and none should until coverage is measured after T5 (\u00a712) and", "  that surface's product owner ratifies a floor \u2014 a people view that opens empty for most companies is", "  worse than no view.", "- **Unverified people are captured, not discarded**, with enough context that identity can be", "  established later without polluting canonical tables now.", "- **Identity is chosen so dedupe stays possible**, by merge, never by retype.", "", "### Non-goals (explicitly out of scope)", "", "- **`doc.doc_entity_map` and person\u2192company attribution.** Unchanged. `Person: {name}` reasons keep", "  pointing at the employer's `corp_id`, no person-keyed rows are written, and the table keeps its", "  three-arm CHECK (`CVW`/`corp_id`, `MVW`/`market_id`, `IVW`/`industry_id`). Changing that would alter", "  article-to-company attribution for every person mention in the corpus \u2014 a blast radius this spec", "  refuses, and a decision worth taking on its own merits later rather than as a side effect here.", "  **One adjacent thing does change, and it is not attribution:** today a document is created only when", "  there is at least one reason, and Event Extraction is enqueued only when a document exists \u2014 so an", "  article whose only match is a person never reaches event extraction at all. T4 makes a stamped", "  person sufficient to create or recover the document and enqueue, while writing nothing to", "  `doc_entity_map`. What an article is *attributed* to is untouched; what gets *processed* is not.", "- **Affiliation edges in the ownership closure.** The edges ship (D6); they do not propagate to", "  event tags. An event about a person is not an event about their employer.", "- **Event-matching logic**, candidate retrieval and scoring. Not touched; see \u00a711 for the", "  interaction with DAT-8299.", "- **`xvw` contact data as a person source.** Ruled out (D9).", "- **Buying or building a public-figure dataset.** People with no verified source enter through", "  the evidence-and-review lane on our own corpus (D2 tier B), not a new data purchase.", "- **Person accounts / hubs.** PVW launches non-account (D7).", "- **Backfill of historical articles.** Forward-only, mirroring the org facet.", "", "---", "", "## 4. Decisions", "", "### D1 \u2014 Identity is ours: an internal person id, with vendor ids as resolution keys", "", "**RATIFIED 2026-08-18.** A person's identity is a **Polaris-owned identifier**. No vendor's id is", "ever the primary key.", "", "Two layers, and the distinction is the whole decision:", "", "| Layer | What it is | Where it lives |", "|---|---|---|", "| **Identity** | Our own person row and its canonical platform UUID. Stable forever, independent of any data provider. | `pvw.persons.id` \u2192 `ent.entities.id` (UUIDv5) |", "| **Resolution keys** | Every external id we have ever seen for that human, one row per source system. Used to decide whether an incoming record is someone we already have. | `pvw.person_source_ids(source_system, source_id) \u2192 person_id` |", "", "**Why not a vendor id as the key.** `ob_exec_id` is The Official Board's executive id. Prospeo is", "a second source, and the source mix will change again. Keying identity on one vendor would mean a", "Prospeo-only person has no identity at all, a vendor swap re-keys the registry, and the same human", "arriving from two vendors becomes two people with no way to say they are one.", "", "**How the resolution table earns its place.** `UNIQUE(source_system, source_id)`, many rows per", "person. Two vendors' ids for the same human are two rows pointing at one `pvw.persons` row \u2014 which", "is exactly how cross-source deduplication gets *expressed* rather than argued about. Adding a", "third source adds rows, never a migration. This mirrors `nvw_match.entities_source_map`, the", "pattern master data already uses for organizations.", "", "**`ob_exec_id` keeps a job \u2014 just not this one.** It becomes the highest-confidence *resolution*", "signal for the Official Board population: match on it, then fall back to name plus employer plus", "title agreement. It is parsed today (`parse_context_fields`, `nvw_match_parsing.py:138`) and used", "nowhere.", "", "**What two mentions being \"the same human\" means, concretely.** Two mentions are the same person", "when they resolve to the same `pvw.persons.id` \u2014 via a shared external id, or via a match the", "resolver made and recorded. Everything else is a candidate (D2), and anything we get wrong is", "correctable by merge (D5), never by re-keying.", "", "**Why not name plus employer as the key.** It fails in both directions: the same person at two", "companies across time becomes two identities, and two same-named officers at one company collapse", "into one. It also bakes an employment fact into a primary key, so a job change forces a merge for", "a person who never changed.", "", "### D2 \u2014 Four states: verified admission, provisional minting, reviewed promotion, and observation", "", "**RATIFIED 2026-08-18.** Officers are admitted from verified sources, and unanchored people \u2014", "celebrities, politicians, athletes, private-company founders \u2014 get a real route in rather than", "sitting in a pile forever.", "", "| Tier | Population | Where they live | How they get in |", "|---|---|---|---|", "| **A \u2014 verified** | Resolves to a verified person source (Official Board, Prospeo, future sources) | `pvw.persons` \u2192 `ent.entities` (`PVW`) | Direct admission; the source is the verification |", "| **B \u2014 provisional** | Unknown to every verified source, but past the evidence bar in our own corpus | `pvw.persons` \u2192 `ent.entities` (`PVW`), `admission_tier = PROVISIONAL` | Minted automatically at the bar (D14). **Links to events; not offered in agent authoring** |", "| **B+ \u2014 evidence-promoted** | A provisional person a reviewer has confirmed | Same row, tier flipped to `EVIDENCE_PROMOTED` | Review (T6). Tier flip only \u2014 canonical id never changes |", "| **C \u2014 observed** | Everyone else: below the bar, one-off, low-confidence | `candidate_person_observations` (DataLake2) | Accumulates evidence toward tier B |", "", "**How the invariant now stands, precisely.** `VERIFIED` rows are source-admitted. `PROVISIONAL` rows", "are admitted automatically by the configured evidence rule and are **unreviewed** \u2014 that is D14's", "narrow, approved relaxation of D8, and it is what lets an unknown person link to events at all.", "`EVIDENCE_PROMOTED` rows have had human review. What never happens at any tier is a canonical row", "appearing because a model named someone once: the evidence bar stands between extraction and", "`pvw.persons`, and the agent-authoring surface is gated to the reviewed tiers (T7).", "", "**Promotion rule (proposed, tune in T6).** A tier-C person becomes eligible when the rollup shows", "sustained, independent evidence: seen in **\u2265 N distinct articles** across **\u2265 2 distinct", "publishers**, spanning **\u2265 M days measured on article publication dates, not processing timestamps**", "\u2014 a replay re-processes old articles now, and processing time would let it manufacture a time span", "that never happened \u2014 with a **stable `(normalized_name, anchor)`** and mention", "confidence above a floor. Eligibility surfaces a review item; it does not admit anyone. Starting", "values need one pass over real rollup data \u2014 deliberately not guessed here.", "", "**Why a threshold at all.** It filters the two failure modes that matter: the misspelling seen", "once, and the generic name that is not a person. Sustained multi-publisher coverage is the cheapest", "available proxy for \"this human is someone our users would want to watch.\"", "", "**What a reviewer sees, and what they own.** The rollup row (name variants, anchors, titles,", "sighting volume, first/last seen, sample evidence spans) and one decision: promote, reject, or", "merge into an existing person. **Open item:** who staffs that queue (\u00a712.7).", "", "**Tier C is not a waiting room with no door.** It is also the measurement surface \u2014 for the first", "time, the size and shape of the people we cannot yet represent becomes countable.", "", "### D3 \u2014 Name is never an identity key for a person", "", "`candidate_business_rollup` dedupes on `normalized_name` alone and accepts that \"Delta\" the", "airline and \"Delta\" the faucets over-merge, because SoS verification splits them later", "(`.docs/codebase/CANDIDATE_ROLLUP_CONTRACT.md`). For people that trade is unacceptable: name", "collision is the norm, not the tail, and no verification backstop exists for tier B.", "", "Therefore:", "", "- The person rollup groups on **`(normalized_name, anchor)`**, where `anchor` is the strongest", "  available co-occurring signal in this order: employer corp \u2192 employer candidate name \u2192", "  geography \u2192 none.", "- The rollup is a **review and volume surface**. It is documented as *not* an identity, and no", "  downstream consumer may treat a rollup row as a person.", "- A tier-B candidate never becomes an `ent.entities` row by accumulating sightings alone.", "", "### D4 \u2014 Context to capture, and why each field is load-bearing", "", "`entity_classification.people` today stores name parts, `is_owner`, `evidence`, `confidence`.", "There is no `context` column \u2014 the org-side context capture never extended to people. Add it,", "with the same additive, fail-safe shape as `organizations.context` (nullable JSONB; NULL on", "historical rows and on capture failure).", "", "**Two homes, not one.** `context` is *per-article* surrounding context \u2014 what this article said", "about this person. Sighting counts and date ranges are *cross-article* aggregates and belong on the", "candidate observations and their rollup, exactly as the org side splits them. Writing a running", "sighting count into a per-article JSONB blob cannot be kept correct, so the split is stated here", "rather than left to the implementer.", "", "**Two sources, and the org analogy only covers one of them.** This is the correction that matters,", "because an earlier draft of this decision listed all the fields as though they assembled the same way.", "", "- **Article-level dimensions** \u2014 geography, industries, who else the article mentioned \u2014 are computed", "  once per article and attached to each entity row. They need nothing from extraction, which is", "  exactly how `organizations.context` works today.", "- **Person-relative facts** \u2014 this person's stated title, this person's employer, the name variants", "  used for them in this article \u2014 are facts about the *person*, not the article. There is nowhere to", "  assemble them from. Today's extraction payload (`common/schemas/entities/people.py`) carries", "  `name`, `evidence`, `confidence` and `is_owner`, and nothing else.", "", "So D4 has a prerequisite: **the extraction payload has to carry the person-relative fields.** That is", "an additive change following the pattern organizations already use \u2014 `OrgTypeAttr` is a per-entity", "typed attribute the LLM fills in, and its own docstring names the extension shape: \"Future typed", "attributes follow the same `XxxAttr(value, evidence)` shape.\" `Person` gains optional", "`title_or_role`, `employer_name` and `aliases` in that shape. `ExtractedEntity` is configured", "`extra=\"ignore\"`, so payloads without them keep parsing and the change is backward-compatible.", "", "**Employer partly works without it, title does not.** Crossing the article's matched organizations", "with a candidate's affiliation edges already yields \"this article names Disney, this candidate is an", "officer of Disney\" \u2014 no new extraction needed. The per-person employer only adds value when an", "article names several companies and the question is which one *this* person belongs to. Title has no", "such workaround: \"as stated in the article\" has exactly one possible source.", "", "**Per-article \u2014 `people.context`:**", "", "| Field | Why it is needed |", "|---|---|", "| `normalized_name` + `normalization_version` | Group sightings; survive a normalization change |", "| Name parts and observed variants / aliases as stated in *this* article | \"Bob Iger\" / \"Robert A. Iger\" are one human; without recorded variants a later merge has no evidence, and D13's adjudicator has nothing to reason over |", "| Title / role as stated in the article | A primary input to D13's deterministic score, and the join to `job_title` in master data |", "| Employer mentions (resolved `corp_id`, plus unresolved names) | The anchor in D3; a D13 score input; also the audit trail for a later affiliation edge |", "| Co-occurring entity refs | Two \"John Smith\" mentions sharing three entities are probably one person; the cheapest disambiguator available, and a D13 score input |", "| Article geography | Disambiguates same-name people; mirrors the business tier |", "| `is_owner`, `confidence` | Already captured on the `people` row; keep them there |", "| Evidence spans | The only human-checkable record of what the article actually said |", "| Any vendor person id the match carries (`ob_exec_id` today) | The resolution key that ties a mention to an existing person (D1); parsed today and discarded |", "", "**Cross-article \u2014 `candidate_person_observations` and its rollup:** first seen, last seen, sighting", "volume, distinct articles, distinct publishers, name variants observed across articles. These are", "the promotion evidence D2 and D14 consume, and the signal for whether an unanchored person matters", "at all. They are computed across rows, so they live where rows aggregate.", "", "**The shared shape is a published contract, with a base.** The org side does not store loose JSONB:", "`entity_classification/schemas/org_context.py` publishes `OrgContext` as a Pydantic read contract", "with `extra=\"forbid\"`, so the writer and its readers cannot drift, and it documents its own null", "semantics and non-guarantees. Person context gets the same treatment, and the two share a base:", "", "- **`ArticleContextBase`** carries the three dimensions that describe *the article* and are", "  identical for every entity mentioned in it: `article_geography`, `industries`,", "  `co_occurring_entities`. `co_occurring_entities` stays in the base even though its value is", "  entity-relative \u2014 \"everyone else on this article\" is one piece of knowledge with a self-exclusion", "  parameter, not two concepts.", "- **`OrgContext`** adds `type_hint`. **`PersonContext`** adds the person fields above. A future type", "  declares its own fields and inherits the envelope.", "", "`assemble_and_write_org_context` already has this seam cut. It reads the article's organization,", "person and location rows in one pass, computes the article-level dimensions under a comment reading", "\"shared across every org on the article\", and builds each row's payload excluding self. Person", "context needs no new reads \u2014 only the loop over `people` instead of `organizations`, and the", "envelope lifted into a shared helper so one definition is computed once.", "", "Refactoring `OrgContext` onto the base does not change stored data. Field order in the serialized", "payload shifts, but the column is JSONB, and per the PostgreSQL docs `jsonb` \"does not preserve", "white space, does not preserve the order of object keys, and does not keep duplicate object keys.\"", "The stored form is identical, so no migration and no reader change.", "", "**One live contract does have to change.** `org_context.PersonRef` deliberately carries **no**", "`platform_entity_id` \u2014 its docstring says the key \"must be absent (not null) for a person ref\". That", "absence is only true while people have no canonical id, which is the thing this epic removes. Adding", "the field is a breaking change under `extra=\"forbid\"`, and the writer's paired comment (\"Persons are", "never stamped with a `platform_entity_id` \u2014 no MatchedEntity join\") marks the exact line. Both land", "in T4.", "", "Storing too little forecloses later merging. The cost of storing more here is schema and a JSONB", "write on a row we already write.", "", "### D5 \u2014 Dedupe later, by merge, never by retype", "", "`entity_type` is immutable on `ent.entities`. Person deduplication uses the shipped primitive:", "`ent.entity_merge_history` with `reason = DEDUP`, victim `superseded_by` survivor. No new", "mechanism is needed, and no person row ever has to be retyped or deleted.", "", "**What a merge does and does not do.** It marks the victim \u2014 sets `superseded_by` / `superseded_on`,", "flips `is_active`, appends one history row. It does **not** rewrite existing references in", "`source_event_entities`, `signal_entities` or `pattern_entities`; merge-aware readers resolve through", "`resolve_terminal_survivor` instead. So \"references redirect\" is true from a reader's point of view", "and false at the row level, and anything written against this epic should say the former.", "", "This is what makes both admission tiers safe. If a verified source turns out to be imperfectly", "resolved, or a reviewer promotes someone we later learn is an existing person under another name,", "the fix is a merge: readers resolve to the survivor, history is audited, and no canonical id is", "destroyed.", "It is also how cross-source duplication resolves when a second vendor's ids arrive (D1).", "", "### D6 \u2014 Affiliation edges are in scope, and excluded from the closure walk", "", "**RATIFIED 2026-08-18.** Person\u2194company relationships are part of this epic. They are stored in", "the existing `ent.entity_relationships` table as a new family, and they do **not** propagate to", "event tags.", "", "**The edges.** A new `AFFILIATION` family with kinds `OFFICER_OF`, `BOARD_MEMBER_OF`,", "`EMPLOYED_BY`; endpoints `PVW \u2192 CVW | BVW`, enforced the same way the existing families enforce", "theirs (denormalized endpoint types kept honest by composite FKs to `ent.entities (id,", "entity_type)`, plus a family CHECK). Master data already holds this: `off_brd.id_match` and", "`refinitiv.ceos` give officer/CEO \u2192 corp, and `nvw_match.entities_context.job_title` gives the", "role. The graph gets who-leads-what without inventing data.", "", "**Why excluded from closure.** Ownership closure is sound for legal hierarchy and brand operation", "because ownership is transitive and the owner genuinely is implicated \u2014 a Twitch event is an", "Amazon event. Employment is not that. A person's death, a criminal charge, or a personal statement", "is not an event about their employer, and the closure would tag it as one at", "`CAUSALLY_IMPLICATED`, materialized as a frozen as-of tag that no later fix can retract from", "historical events. `ASSOCIATIVE` edges already get exactly this treatment for the same reason.", "", "**What the edges are for, then.** Four things, none of which needs closure:", "", "1. **\"Show me the people we have for this company.\"** The query exists after T5; the surface does", "   not ship in this epic (\u00a73). A caller asks the edge table in reverse: every `PVW` entity with an active `AFFILIATION` edge whose target is this", "   corp's canonical entity. One indexed lookup \u2014", "   `idx_ent_entity_relationships_target` already exists for exactly this direction \u2014 returning", "   people with their role kind and, through their own entity id, the events they are linked to.", "   This is the capability the registry unlocks that master data cannot: today the officer\u2192corp", "   relationship exists in `off_brd` / `refinitiv` but the people on the other end are not entities,", "   so there is nothing to link to or click through to.", "2. The relationship graph itself \u2014 who leads what, current and previous affiliation, board overlap.", "3. Person profile and event-context surfaces.", "4. Future compile-time scope expansion, where an *agent author* can choose to pull in a company's", "   executives \u2014 an opt-in authoring decision, not a silent tag on every event.", "", "Note how (1) and closure exclusion coexist: the account team **sees** the company's people and can", "follow them to their events, while an event about one of those people is still not tagged as an", "event about the company. Visibility is a query; tagging is an assertion. Only the second one is", "wrong.", "", "**What is not lost.** The employer already gets its coverage: a person mention still produces the", "CVW `Person: {name}` / `Entity CEO: {name}` attribution in `doc_entity_map`, unchanged. Keeping", "closure out of affiliation removes nothing that exists today.", "", "### D7 \u2014 PVW launches non-account, account-capable", "", "Mirrors decision K of the org facet. `ent.entities.entity_type` *is* the `AccountType` enum, so", "adding `PVW` makes it account-capable by construction; no `acc.accounts` row, no hub, and no", "person-account UX is created. Person accounts later would be an opt-in build, not a schema", "rework.", "", "### D8 \u2014 No *unevidenced* LLM output enters `pvw.persons`", "", "**Amended by D14.** As originally written this decision said a row exists only because a source or a", "reviewer said so. D14 adds a third route \u2014 automatic provisional minting at an evidence bar \u2014 so the", "rule is now:", "", "A row in `pvw.persons` exists for exactly one of three reasons: a verified person source says the", "person exists (`VERIFIED`); the configured evidence rule admitted them provisionally (`PROVISIONAL`,", "unreviewed \u2014 D14's approved relaxation); or a reviewer confirmed a provisional person", "(`EVIDENCE_PROMOTED`). What never happens at any tier is a person row appearing because a model named", "someone once \u2014 the evidence bar is the floor, and the reviewed tiers are the only ones an agent can", "author against (T7).", "", "### D9 \u2014 ExecView's Official Board population is the seed; a deduplicated spine is still required", "", "**AMENDED 2026-08-18 in review. The schema question \u2014 where the spine lives \u2014 is RESOLVED in D11", "(`PVW` code, `pvw` schema).**", "", "An earlier draft claimed ExecView contact data was the wrong *data class* for a person registry and", "should not seed it. **That was wrong for the company-affiliated population.** ExecView (`xvw`, code", "module `accelerate_models/kads/`) is an active production service, and its Official Board feed is", "the closest thing the platform has to a canonical set of company-affiliated people.", "", "What an Official Board card carries in `person_info` (`kads/app/utils/constants.py`):", "", "| Field | Meaning | Why the registry wants it |", "|---|---|---|", "| `OBEXEC` | Official Board Executive ID | The external person key \u2014 same id space as `nvw_match.entities.context.ob_exec_id` |", "| `OBEXCS` | All Related OB Executive IDs | **Populated on zero cards** (\u00a77.2) \u2014 defined, unused |", "| `OBCOMP` / `OBPACO` / `OBULCO` | Company / parent company / ultimate company | Affiliation edges, with the ownership context |", "| `OBHIRE` / `OBQUIT` / `OBNLWC` | First entry date / quitting date / no longer with company | Time bounds where present: `OBHIRE` 22.7%, `OBQUIT` 5.4%, `OBNLWC` **zero** (\u00a77.2) |", "| `OBBOSS` | Boss ID | Reporting line |", "| `PIOIDS` / `KPIOID` | Related Polaris IO ids with level / KAD Polaris IO id | **Absent on every OB card** (\u00a77.2); only client-submitted cards carry it |", "", "The OB feed is the `xvw.data_sources` row named **`ExecView`** (id 20, `3RD PARTY`, not", "client-scoped); **`Pegasus`** (id 58) is Prospeo. Client visibility is gated through", "`xvw.linked_sources (client_id, data_source_id)`. No source is literally named \"The Official", "Board\" \u2014 that string appears only in API sample data.", "", "**Consequences, and they improve the design:**", "", "- **The seed comes from the OB population, not from a parallel read of `nvw_match`** (T3). It is", "  richer and closer to source.", "- **Affiliation edges seed from `OBCOMP` / `OBPACO` / `OBULCO` with `OBHIRE` / `OBQUIT` /", "  `OBNLWC`** (T5) \u2014 time-bounded and deactivatable, which `off_brd.id_match` + `refinitiv.ceos`", "  alone would not give.", "- **The news side and the OB feed already share a person key.** `context.ob_exec_id` on a matched", "  person mention and `OBEXEC` on an ExecView card are the same id space, so one registry identity", "  serves both without a fuzzy join. This is what `person_source_ids` exists for (D1).", "- **Prospeo shares no key with OB.** Pegasus cards carry no `OBEXEC`, so cross-source resolution", "  needs a matching pass on name + company + email/LinkedIn \u2014 the same shape as the existing", "  `client_people_matches` weighted match. Real work in T3, not a lookup (\u00a77.2).", "", "**The one structural fact that does not bend.** `ent.entities` requires a typed FK to a table with", "**one row per canonical thing**. `xvw.people_cards` is one row per *(person, data source)* \u2014 the", "same human from Official Board and from a client's Salesforce feed is two cards, and `OBEXCS`", "exists precisely because one human can carry several OB ids. An FK to `people_cards.id` would mint", "one `ent.entities` row per card, which is the exact duplication the registry exists to prevent.", "**A deduplicated person spine is therefore required regardless of which schema it lives in** \u2014 the", "same reason `ent.entities` exists rather than pointing at raw source rows.", "", "**What is still true about contact data.** Cards carry email, phone numbers and LinkedIn, and card", "*visibility* is client-entitled through `linked_sources`. The spine takes the identity and", "affiliation fields and leaves the contact PII in ExecView, where it is served under the", "entitlements that already govern it. That is a projection boundary, not a data-class judgement", "about the service.", "", "**What is still out of scope.** Deduplicating cards for ExecView's own purposes; any registry\u2192card", "contact-data exposure; and a card\u2194person link surfaced in the contact product. All reasonable", "later, none needed here.", "", "**Corp hubs will end up with two people surfaces**, and that is fine as long as the labels are", "honest: ExecView contacts (who you can reach, client-entitled) and registry people (who leads and", "who is in the news, platform-wide, event-linked). Worth a note to whoever designs that hub.", "", "### D10 \u2014 One person table for company-tied and unaffiliated people", "", "**RATIFIED 2026-08-18.** `pvw.persons` holds both populations \u2014 the officers and executives tied", "to a company, and the \"any person\" population. Not two tables, not a subtype.", "", "**Why one table.** A person is the same kind of thing whether or not they currently hold a", "corporate role, and the two populations are not disjoint over time. An athlete who buys a team, a", "founder whose company enters master data, a politician who joins a board: with two tables, each of", "those is a migration between stores and a broken canonical id. With one table plus an edge, it is", "an edge insert and nothing downstream notices.", "", "Which population a row belongs to is expressed by two things that can both change without", "re-keying the person:", "", "- **`admission_tier`** \u2014 how they got in (`VERIFIED` from a person source, `EVIDENCE_PROMOTED` by", "  review). Tells a reader how much to trust the row.", "- **Affiliation edges** \u2014 whether they are currently tied to a company, and how (`OFFICER_OF`,", "  `BOARD_MEMBER_OF`, `EMPLOYED_BY`).", "", "Those are orthogonal on purpose. An evidence-promoted person can be an officer; a verified officer", "can leave and hold no affiliation at all. Neither transition touches identity.", "", "### D11 \u2014 The type code is permanent; the schema is not. Choose accordingly.", "", "**RATIFIED 2026-08-18.** `PVW` as the `AccountType` code, `pvw` as the schema \u2014 decided by", "separating what is irreversible from what is cosmetic.", "", "**The code is baked into every person id, forever.** Canonical ids are computed as", "`uuid5(NAMESPACE_PLATFORM_ENTITY, f\"{entity_type.value}:{backing_id}\")`", "(`common/constants/platform_entities.py:19`), and `entity_type` is immutable on `ent.entities` by", "design. Changing the code later re-keys every person entity and needs a merge/supersede pass over", "the whole population. So the code must describe the population accurately and permanently.", "", "`PVW` (PersonView) does. `XVW` (ExecView) would not: under D2 tier B the registry holds athletes,", "defendants and politicians who will never be executives, and the label would misdescribe them in", "every id and friendly-name mapping the platform has. The PRD's own type name is PERSON/PVW; only", "its `xvw_id` column suggestion pointed the other way, and that is the reversible half.", "", "**The schema is not an input to that function.** Relocating the table later is `ALTER TABLE \u2026 SET", "SCHEMA`, a re-pointed FK, and one settings variable. No canonical id changes; no stored", "`entity_id` anywhere changes, because every consumer references `ent.entities.id`. So `pvw` is", "chosen by convention \u2014 the AccountType code names the schema, and the schema holds exactly one", "canonical table \u2014 and it can be revisited cheaply if people should later be consolidated.", "", "**Two corrections that removed the apparent stakes:**", "", "- **There is no release-cadence coupling.** Accelerate has one `alembic.ini` and one `versions/`", "  directory \u2014 362 migrations spanning `xvw` (44), `ent` (15), `bvw`, `intel`, `acc`. Same repo,", "  same chain, same deploy, wherever the table lives.", "- **Cross-schema FKs are the norm**, not a compromise: `ent.entities` already points at", "  `cvw.corporations`, `mvw.markets`, `ivw.industries`, `bvw.businesses`, `brv.brands`.", "", "**If one people home is wanted later**, an `xvw.persons` view over `pvw.persons` provides it at", "zero cost \u2014 no duplication, no identity implications, no migration.", "", "**What would justify revisiting the schema:** if ExecView's owners take on day-to-day maintenance", "of the spine (loaders, dedupe sweeps, OB refresh), co-locating it in `xvw` is a fair signal of that", "ownership. Schema location only signals ownership; it does not enforce it, so the spine can be", "assigned to whoever should own it and stay in `pvw`.", "", "### D12 \u2014 Seed the full Official Board population, behind a scale gate", "", "**RATIFIED 2026-08-19.** The registry admits every person in the Official Board feed", "(~491,310), not only the 20,145 that master data can currently match from article text.", "", "**Why breadth wins.** The corp-hub people view (D6) is a stated goal and is worthless at 4%", "coverage \u2014 most companies would surface nobody. A registry person no article mentions costs", "nothing: it behaves exactly like a corporation nobody writes about. And matchability can be grown", "later \u2014 extend `master_text`, or match extracted names against the registry directly \u2014 with no", "re-seed, because canonical ids derive from `(entity_type, backing_id)` and never move (D11).", "", "**Licence confirmed** by the system owner: copying OB identities into the tenant-agnostic registry", "is permitted.", "", "**The gate.** Seeding takes `ent.entities` from ~1,960 rows to ~493,000, making people 99.6% of the", "registry. The agent-facing resolver has no index on `display_name` and falls back to a", "leading-wildcard `ILIKE`, so it degrades from a trivial scan to a full scan plus sort on every call", "(\u00a77.5). **T8 lands before T3's seed runs** \u2014 the index, the minimum-length guard, and a measured", "benchmark are a precondition of the seed, not a follow-up.", "", "**What \"don't break agents querying entities\" means concretely**, and both are T8/T7 acceptance", "criteria rather than intentions: resolver latency at 493k rows stays within an agreed bound of the", "current p95, and no existing entity-resolution result changes because people were added.", "", "### D13 \u2014 Every registry person must be matchable, and people invert the over-attribution default", "", "**RATIFIED 2026-08-19.** A person who cannot be linked to an event is not delivering the capability", "this epic exists for. Seeding ~491k people that only 4% of the corpus can reach is not acceptable", "(\u00a77.4), so matching is in scope as first-class ticket work (T4), not a downstream hope.", "", "**Why they are unmatchable today.** Matching runs `nvw_match.master_text` \u2192", "`text_match_xref` \u2192 `nvw_match.entities`. Master data carries officers of the companies we track as", "CVW corporations (~1,711); the Official Board feed covers officers of far more companies than we", "track. The 20,145 matchable people are not a subset chosen by accident \u2014 they are a different", "population boundary.", "", "**The obvious fix is a trap.** Loading the missing ~471k names into `master_text` would make them", "matchable with no pipeline change \u2014 and would be a precision disaster. The matcher deliberately", "**keeps every match**: `_dedupe_matches_by_normalized_name` retains one match per corp, and", "`ENTITY_MATCHING.md` states the principle outright \u2014 \"over-attribution is preferred over silently", "dropping a company's coverage.\" One \"John Smith\" in an article would link every John Smith in the", "registry to that event.", "", "**People invert that default.** Over-attributing a company means an article shows up in an account", "view that did not need it. Over-attributing a *person* means asserting that a named human did", "something they did not do \u2014 appearing in their profile, their event history, and any agent watching", "them. **For people, prefer a miss to a wrong match.** This is a deliberate exception to the house", "convention, and it is the reason person matching is a disambiguation design rather than a", "name-loading exercise.", "", "**The matching rule \u2014 cheap deterministic bands, with an LLM adjudicating the gray zone.**", "", "This is the platform's existing shape for exactly this problem, not a new mechanism. Three places", "already do it: event matching scores candidates and routes the middle band to `NEEDS_LLM`", "(`event_synthesis/services/scoring/composite.py`); L2 dedup runs a cheap LLM on two margin windows", "plus an explicit mid-band (`web_extraction/services/helpers/borderline_verifier.py`); and Signal", "folding does the same under UNI-18333. Person disambiguation joins that pattern.", "", "A cheap deterministic score is computed per (extracted name, candidate registry person) from the", "signals D4 already captures \u2014 name-match strength, employer agreement, title agreement, and overlap", "between the article's co-occurring entities and the person's affiliation edges.", "", "**Title agreement needs a title on both sides, and the registry side is the thin one.** The article", "side comes from D4's new `title_or_role`. The registry side has no home today: `pvw.persons` holds no", "title, and `nvw_match.entities_context.job_title` covers only the ~20,145 already-matchable people.", "The Official Board card carries `TITLE`, and a title is a fact about a *role at a company* rather than", "about a person, so it belongs on the affiliation edge \u2014 **T5 carries OB `TITLE` onto the edge as a", "role title**, and the scorer reads it from there with `job_title` as fallback. Without that, title", "agreement cannot fire for ~471k of the registry and the feature is decorative. The score decides", "one of three outcomes:", "", "| Band | Condition | Outcome |", "|---|---|---|", "| **Confident match** | Score at or above the high boundary \u2014 the name matches and the article corroborates it | Match, no LLM call |", "| **Gray zone** | Score between the boundaries \u2014 a plausible match the deterministic signals cannot settle. Includes the single-candidate-unique-name case and the several-candidates-one-weakly-favoured case | **Adjudicate.** `gpt-5.6-luna` sees the article context and the candidate people and answers which one, or none |", "| **Confident non-match** | Score below the low boundary \u2014 several candidates with nothing to separate them, or no plausible candidate | No match, no LLM call |", "", "**The fail-safe direction is declared per band, and it is what makes \"prefer a miss\" real.** In the", "gray zone, an LLM failure or an unparseable verdict resolves to **no match** \u2014 never to the", "highest-scoring candidate. The `borderline_verifier` sets this precedent explicitly: it biases each", "band toward the safer classification \"rather than falling through to the vector score the verifier", "was built to second-guess.\" For people the safer direction is always no match.", "", "**\"None of them\" is a first-class answer.** The registry is incomplete by construction \u2014 491k", "corporate officers, not every human. So a name can be unique among the people we hold while the", "article is about someone we have never heard of. An adjudicator that could only pick a candidate", "would match that article to the wrong human. Being able to decline is the point, and it is why a", "unique name is a gray-zone input rather than an automatic match.", "", "**Why this shape rather than a fixed tier rule.** Corroboration becomes graded instead of binary: a", "weak-but-real signal is adjudicated rather than discarded. It also gives the name-variant problem a", "natural home \u2014 \"Bob Iger\" against \"Robert A. Iger\" is what a language model gets right and exact", "normalization gets wrong \u2014 which is what closes that open item rather than deferring it.", "", "**D4 and D6 are load-bearing here, not nice-to-have.** The employer anchor, the co-occurring", "entities and the title are both the deterministic score's inputs and the adjudicator's evidence. An", "epic that shipped people without them would have nothing to score and nothing to show the LLM.", "", "**Every non-match is recorded, not silent.** A confident non-match and a gray-zone decline both land", "in `candidate_person_observations` with the candidate set they were chosen from, so the decline rate", "is measurable per band and the boundaries can be tuned against evidence.", "", "**One case the schema cannot separate, and how it resolves.** `entity_classification.people` holds one", "row per name per article \u2014 the same constraint `organizations` has, and two same-named subjects in a", "single article are about as rare for people as two same-named companies are. Where it does happen, the", "mentions merge into one row whose evidence may be internally inconsistent: two different stated titles,", "or two different employers. **That inconsistency is itself a signal, and D13 declines on it** rather", "than picking whichever candidate scores highest. This is the one place people genuinely part company", "with organizations \u2014 the business rollup accepts over-merge because SoS verification splits it later,", "and people have no such backstop \u2014 but it costs a rule, not a schema change.", "", "**Two constraints on the implementation, both hard.**", "", "- **The boundaries are derived, not guessed.** They are set from the \u00a77.6 measurement and the", "  observed decline rate, and they are configuration \u2014 the same treatment", "  `DEDUP_VERIFIER_MID_BAND_LOW` / `_HIGH` already get. No constant is compiled in.", "- **The adjudication call sits outside the L1 transaction window.** `entity_classification.py`", "  Phase A holds a Datalake write session, a master read session and an Accelerate read session open", "  together across steps 1\u20136b, and this project's critical invariant forbids external I/O inside that", "  window. The LLM call must be structured like the existing step-7 sync I/O \u2014 after those sessions", "  commit and release their locks \u2014 or it holds locks across a network call. This is the single", "  easiest thing to get wrong in the ticket and it is called out again in T4.", "", "### D14 \u2014 Unknown people get a provisional entity, so events can link before verification", "", "**RATIFIED 2026-08-19.** An unknown person crossing an evidence bar is minted as a **provisional**", "registry entity \u2014 a real `pvw.persons` row and a real `ent.entities` PVW row \u2014 so events link to", "them immediately. Verification promotes the tier; it does not create the entity.", "", "**The problem this fixes, and it is not only ours.** Today a candidate is an observation row with no", "canonical id (`candidate_observations` has no `platform_entity_id` column). A small-business", "candidate seen fifty times still cannot be attached to a single event, because", "`build_known_entity_refs` drops anything with a NULL `platform_entity_id`. The org epic accepted", "that on the promise of SoS verification. The people population has no SoS, so accepting it here", "would mean unknown people never link to events at all \u2014 which is not an acceptable outcome for a", "capability whose whole point is linking people to events.", "", "**Two populations that must not be treated alike.** This is the carve-out, and getting it wrong", "would be worse than the gap:", "", "| Case | Situation | Behaviour |", "|---|---|---|", "| **Unknown person** | The name matches nobody in the registry | Mint provisional once the evidence bar is met. Events link from then on |", "| **Ambiguous known person** | The name matches registry people the article cannot separate \u2014 a confident non-match, or a gray-zone decline (D13) | **Never mint.** Minting a 41st \"John Smith\" beside 40 real ones manufactures a duplicate of a person we already have, and links the event to a fiction. Fail closed, record the observation |", "", "The distinction is \"we don't know who this is\" versus \"we know several people it could be.\" Only", "the first is solved by creating an entity.", "", "**The evidence bar, not first sighting.** Minting on first mention would fill the registry with", "misspellings, one-off names and extraction noise \u2014 the org measurement found ~14% junk in the", "comparable company bucket. So provisional minting fires at the D2 threshold (distinct articles,", "distinct publishers, time span, stable name+anchor). **Linking is forward-only from that point.**", "Sightings recorded before the bar stay as candidate evidence and are not retroactively linked to", "their events: `candidate_person_observations` records which *article* a person appeared in, not which", "raw event or what role they held, and event extraction never saw a person reference for those", "articles. Recovering those links would need an event-extraction replay, which is out of scope here", "(T6).", "", "**What a provisional entity can and cannot do.** This is what keeps the registry honest and answers", "the agent-surface concern directly:", "", "| Surface | Provisional | Verified / evidence-promoted |", "|---|---|---|", "| Linked to events (`source_event_entities`) | **Yes** | Yes |", "| Resolvable in agent authoring (`resolve_entity`) | **No** \u2014 filtered by tier | Yes |", "| Listed on a corp hub via affiliation | Yes, marked provisional | Yes |", "| Deduplicated by merge if later found to be an existing person | Yes | Yes |", "", "Promotion is a **tier flip on the same row**, so the canonical id never changes and no event link", "has to be rewritten. If a provisional person turns out to be someone we already had, the merge", "primitive makes merge-aware readers resolve to the survivor (D5).", "", "**This relaxes a stated invariant, with the invariant owner's approval.** The org epic's \u00a73 rule", "reads \"No LLM output enters canonical / 'official' tables\u2026 Promotion is never direct from", "extraction.\" A provisional entity is extraction-derived and does sit in `ent.entities`. The", "invariant's *purpose* \u2014 keeping unverified noise out of the surfaces people trust \u2014 is preserved by", "the evidence bar plus tier gating on the agent-facing path. Its *letter* is not.", "**Approved by the org-epic owner on 2026-08-19**, so the relaxation is sanctioned rather than a", "unilateral exception. It applies to this epic; extending it to business candidates is a separate", "change (below).", "", "**Businesses should get the same treatment.** Nothing here is people-specific: an SMB candidate seen", "across ten articles has the same claim to a provisional entity, and the org epic would gain the", "same capability. Out of scope for this epic to implement, but the mechanism is deliberately built", "type-agnostic so that follow-up is a configuration of the same machinery, not a rebuild. Worth", "raising with the org-epic owner.", "", "---", "", "## 5. Registry shape", "", "### 5.1 `pvw.persons` and `pvw.person_source_ids`", "", "New schema `pvw` (PersonView), separate from ExecView's `xvw` per D9 \u2014 different job, different", "data class, different tenancy. It also keeps the convention every other bridged type follows: the", "AccountType code names the schema, and the schema holds exactly one canonical table", "(`cvw.corporations`, `mvw.markets`, `ivw.industries`, `bvw.businesses`, `brv.brands`).", "", "Two tables, because identity and provenance are different things (D1).", "", "**`pvw.persons` \u2014 who exists.** Follows the `bvw.businesses` / `brv.brands` precedent (thin table,", "ids minted by the loader), with one required departure: **no unique constraint on name.**", "", "| Column | Notes |", "|---|---|", "| `id` | Integer surrogate PK, minted by the seed/reconciliation job. Ours; carries no vendor semantics |", "| `display_name` | Best-known full name. Representative, never an identity |", "| `admission_tier` | `PROVISIONAL` (minted at the D14 evidence bar), `VERIFIED` (from a person source), or `EVIDENCE_PROMOTED` (a reviewed provisional, D2 tier B). Current trust state, not only how they got in \u2014 a provisional person later found in a verified source becomes `VERIFIED` without rewriting the original admission provenance |", "| `admitted_on`, `admitted_by` | Provenance of the admission decision; `admitted_by` NULL for automated verified-source loads. A provisional person later found in a verified source has their tier raised without these being rewritten |", "| `normalized_name` + `normalization_version` | **Required, with an index.** D13 resolves an extracted name against ~491k rows on every article; without a stored normalized form and an index on it there is no lookup, only a scan. The version is what lets a normalization change be rolled forward without silently re-partitioning the registry |", "", "**Where the platform-wide person UUID comes from.** `ent.entities.id` \u2014 the UUIDv5 over the pinned", "platform namespace and `(PVW, pvw.persons.id)`. That UUID is the person identifier every other", "service already knows how to hold: `source_event_entities.entity_id`, `signal_entities.entity_id`,", "`pattern_entities.entity_id` are all `ent.entities.id`. So the integer stays an internal", "schema-convention key (the typed FK columns on `ent.entities` are all `Integer`), and the durable,", "exchangeable person id is the UUID \u2014 same as it already is for a corporation.", "", "**One limit on that stability, stated so nobody over-promises it.** The UUID is derived from the", "person's integer id, and that id is sequence-allocated. So it is stable across reruns, retries and", "refreshes *within* a registry \u2014 a `pvw.persons` row is never deleted or re-keyed \u2014 but an", "independently rebuilt environment will not reproduce the same person UUIDs unless the backing ids are", "replicated from the authoritative registry. That is true of every bridged type here, not just people;", "it is called out because \u00a75.1 previously implied cross-environment stability it cannot deliver.", "", "**`pvw.person_source_ids` \u2014 where we have seen them.** The resolution layer, and the reason no", "vendor owns our identity.", "", "| Column | Notes |", "|---|---|", "| `person_id` | FK \u2192 `pvw.persons.id` |", "| `source_system` | `OFFICIAL_BOARD`, `PROSPEO`, `NVW_MATCH`, \u2026 \u2014 extend by adding rows, never a migration |", "| `source_id` | That system's id for this human (e.g. an `ob_exec_id`) |", "| `is_primary` | Optional marker for the record we prefer for display refresh; at most one active primary per person |", "| `is_active` | A vendor id can be withdrawn without deleting the resolution history. Resolution reads active rows only |", "| `first_seen_on`, `last_seen_on` | When this external id was first and last observed for this person |", "| `PRIMARY KEY (source_system, source_id)` | One external id resolves to exactly one person. Stated as the primary key rather than a bare unique constraint so migration authors do not have to infer it |", "", "Many rows per person is the point: two vendors' ids for one human are two rows pointing at one", "person, which is how cross-source dedup is *expressed*. A vendor swap deprecates a", "`source_system`; it never re-keys the registry.", "", "### 5.2 `ent.entities`", "", "- New `AccountType` value `PVW`; friendly names follow the existing maps (`PersonView` /", "  `Person`).", "- New nullable typed FK `person_id \u2192 pvw.persons.id ON DELETE RESTRICT`.", "- Extend `entities_typed_fk_chk` with the `PVW` arm (`person_id NOT NULL`, all other typed FKs", "  NULL).", "- New partial unique index `idx_ent_entities_pvw_person` on `(entity_type, person_id) WHERE", "  person_id IS NOT NULL`.", "- `id` = UUIDv5 over the pinned platform namespace and `(entity_type, backing_source_id)`,", "  identical to the other five types, so a person's canonical id is stable across reseeds and refreshes", "  within a registry. It is **not** reproducible in an independently rebuilt environment unless the", "  backing ids are replicated \u2014 see \u00a75.1; the same is true of every bridged type.", "- INSERT/UPDATE triggers on `pvw.persons` materialize and rename the `ent.entities` row;", "  idempotent backfill on rerun.", "- `resolve_platform_entity_id` gains its `AccountType.PVW \u2192 PlatformEntity.person_id` map entry", "  (`common/db/operations/entities.py:_backing_column`). That is the whole resolver change \u2014", "  the DataLake2 stamping wrapper is already type-agnostic", "  (`entity_classification/services/helpers/platform_entity_resolution.py`).", "", "### 5.3 Verdict on the PVW blueprint in the Signal Engine PRD", "", "**Amend.** Two halves, two verdicts:", "", "- **Mechanism \u2014 adopt as written.** \"A canonical person table and an FK column on", "  `ent.entities` following the same trigger-and-backfill pattern\" (PRD \u00a73.4) is exactly right,", "  and BVW/BRV have since proven it twice.", "- **Premise \u2014 replace.** \"People are referenced via XVW today through `data_source_id`\" points", "  at the client contact-card subsystem. Naming the future FK `xvw_id` would hard-code that wrong", "  source into the schema. The person source is the master-data person population (D1); the", "  column is `person_id` and the schema is `pvw`.", "", "Also stale in the same paragraph and worth an errata pass on v1.9: `ent.entities` admits five", "types, not three; merge history exists. Two further PRD lines follow from PVW landing:", "\"PERSON/PVW entities are not routed in MVP\" (\u00a7 Layer 1) and the resolver's people-centric", "capability warning (\u00a7 agent authoring).", "", "---", "", "### 5.4 The affiliation edge family", "", "Added to the existing `ent.entity_relationships` table \u2014 no new store (D6).", "", "| Aspect | Value |", "|---|---|", "| `relationship_family` | `AFFILIATION` (new value) |", "| `relationship_kind` | `OFFICER_OF`, `BOARD_MEMBER_OF`, `EMPLOYED_BY` (new values) |", "| Endpoints | `source_entity_type = PVW`, `target_entity_type \u2208 {CVW, BVW}` |", "| Enforcement | Family CHECK on the denormalized endpoint types, kept honest by the existing composite FKs to `ent.entities (id, entity_type)` |", "| Closure | **Excluded.** The walker follows `LEGAL_HIERARCHY` and `BRAND_OPERATION` only |", "| Direction | Follows the table's ownerward convention: the person is `source`, the organization is `target` |", "| Seed | `off_brd.subsidiaries` (85% of the matchable population, \u00a77.1), `off_brd.id_match` (officer/board \u2192 corp), `refinitiv.ceos` (CEO \u2192 corp), role from `nvw_match.entities_context.job_title`; loaded with `managed_by_seed = TRUE` so seed maintenance can never deactivate a producer-written edge |", "| Target resolution | **`OBCOMP` is an Official Board company id with no bridge into our corp id space** \u2014 `KPIOID` is absent on every OB card (\u00a77.2), so the hoped-for existing link does not exist. Resolve the target in order: any authoritative OB-company\u2192`corp_id` mapping; then the master-side `ob_exec_id \u2192 corp_id` pairs, which is what `off_brd.subsidiaries` / `off_brd.id_match` already are; then an exact normalized company-name match that yields **exactly one** active CVW/BVW entity. Zero matches and multiple matches both mean **keep the person, write no edge**, counted separately as a miss and as an ambiguity so the two are distinguishable. Never mint a corporation from `OBCOMP` |", "| Refresh | Deactivating `managed_by_seed` edges absent from a feed is permitted **only after a complete source read**. A partial or failed read must never deactivate, or a truncated feed silently drops valid affiliations. `OBNLWC` cannot drive deactivation \u2014 it is populated on zero cards (\u00a77.2); use `OBQUIT` where present, otherwise absence-on-complete-refresh |", "| Lifecycle | Mutable and always-current, like every other family; `is_active` for soft delete. T5 adds nullable `effective_from` / `effective_to` DATE columns with a CHECK that `effective_to` is NULL or not earlier than `effective_from`. OB's dates are thin \u2014 `OBHIRE` 22.7%, `OBQUIT` 5.4%, `OBNLWC` zero (\u00a77.2) \u2014 so missing dates stay NULL and never block an active edge |", "| Tenure depth | **One tenure per `(person, company, kind)`.** The table's unique triple cannot hold two stints, so a rehire updates the existing edge rather than appending. The graph answers current and previous affiliation, not a career history. Modelling full tenure history would mean breaking that triple, which is the property that made this table the right home in the first place |", "", "Cycle flagging does not apply \u2014 a person\u2194organization edge set cannot form a cycle within the", "family, and the family is closure-excluded regardless.", "", "## 6. End-to-end flow after this lands", "", "```", "verified person sources (Official Board, Prospeo, \u2026)", "  \u2514\u2500 resolve via pvw.person_source_ids \u2192 pvw.persons (VERIFIED)               [T3]", "     \u2514\u2500 trigger \u2192 ent.entities (PVW, UUIDv5)                                  [T1]", "        \u2514\u2500 affiliation edges: person --OFFICER_OF--> corp (closure-excluded)   [T5]", "", "article", "  \u2514\u2500 AI Questionnaire L1: people extracted (name, is_owner, evidence, confidence)", "     \u2514\u2500 EC L1 pass 1: collect candidates, choose nobody yet                    [T4]", "        \u251c\u2500 from nvw_match.entities (context.type = person)", "        \u2514\u2500 from pvw.persons via normalized name", "     \u2514\u2500 EC L1: organizations, locations, industries matched; context assembled [T2]", "     \u2514\u2500 EC L1 pass 2 \u2014 one person decision, after the write scope commits      [T4]", "        \u251c\u2500 confident match      \u2192 people.platform_entity_id = <PVW uuid>", "        \u251c\u2500 gray zone            \u2192 gpt-5.6-luna adjudicates \u2192 that person, or none", "        \u2514\u2500 confident non-match  \u2192 no link; candidate_person_observations       [T2]", "                                   \u2514\u2500 evidence bar \u2192 provisional mint          [T6]", "                                      \u2514\u2500 review \u2192 EVIDENCE_PROMOTED            [T6]", "", "           Event extraction: person refs enter the prompt as P1..Pn            [T4]", "              \u2514\u2500 raw_events.entities_involved: {entity_id, entity_type:\"PVW\",", "                 role, confidence, provenance:{person_ids:[...]}}              [T4]", "                 \u2514\u2500 ESS: bridged-type set admits PVW \u2192 source_event_entities   [T4]", "                    \u2514\u2500 Signal Engine: PVW in scope + signal_entities           [T7]", "```", "", "**Where the person id is stored, and why not on the match row.** `people.platform_entity_id`, not", "`matched_entities.platform_entity_id`. `matched_entities.master_text_id` and `nvw_entity_id` are both", "`NOT NULL`, and a person resolved against the registry rather than through `nvw_match.master_text`", "has neither \u2014 which is ~471k of the ~491k seeded people, the entire population T4's matching tier", "exists to reach. This is not a workaround: `entity_classification.locations` already carries", "`platform_entity_id` directly on its own row and has no `matched_entity_id` at all, so people follow", "the locations precedent. Person-originated `matched_entities` rows stay NULL-stamped and keep serving", "the existing CVW `Person: {name}` attribution, unchanged.", "", "**What is and is not already type-agnostic.** From `source_event_entities` rightward the *data plane*", "is: `source_event_entities.entity_id` is a plain FK to `ent.entities.id` with no type constraint,", "`resolve_platform_entity_id_or_skip` is an existence check, and Signal Engine reads the type off", "`ent.entities` rather than gating on it. The *producer* path stays type-aware in three DataLake2", "places, not two \u2014 prompt projection, the provenance-key map, and the ESS bridged-type allowlist (all", "T4). The *authoring* path stays type-aware in the projection, the resolver, the setup prompt and the", "direct-UUID scope validator (all T7).", "", "---", "", "## 7. Measurement gate (T0)", "", "Four read-only queries against master data. They size the person population, discover which", "external id spaces exist in it, and measure how duplicated it is. Nothing here blocks T1, T2, T5 or", "T7 \u2014 it gates the seed and resolution design (T3).", "", "Run against the master database. Q4 joins `cvw.corporations`; if that lives apart from", "`nvw_match`, run Q4 where `cvw` is reachable and drop the join elsewhere.", "", "```sql", "-- Q1. Discover the id spaces. Which context keys do person entities actually carry?", "--     This is how we learn whether Prospeo (or anything else) is already present alongside", "--     The Official Board, rather than assuming ob_exec_id is the only vendor key.", "SELECT k                       AS context_key,", "       count(*)                AS person_rows_with_key,", "       count(DISTINCT e.context->>k) AS distinct_values", "FROM nvw_match.entities e", "CROSS JOIN LATERAL jsonb_object_keys(e.context) AS k", "WHERE jsonb_typeof(e.context) = 'object'      -- jsonb_object_keys errors on a non-object", "  AND e.context->>'type' = 'person'", "GROUP BY 1", "ORDER BY 2 DESC;", "", "-- Q2. Population and provenance mix.", "SELECT e.original_id->'id'->>'table'                    AS source_table,", "       count(*)                                         AS entity_rows,", "       count(*) FILTER (WHERE e.context ? 'ob_exec_id') AS with_ob_exec_id", "FROM nvw_match.entities e", "WHERE e.context->>'type' = 'person'", "GROUP BY 1", "ORDER BY 2 DESC;", "", "-- Q3. How duplicated is the population, measured against the best available external id?", "--     Many rows per id => the resolver collapses master duplicates on the way in.", "--     One row per id   => master data is already resolved; the seed is close to a copy.", "WITH p AS (", "  SELECT e.id, e.context->>'ob_exec_id' AS ext_id", "  FROM nvw_match.entities e", "  WHERE e.context->>'type' = 'person'", "    AND e.context->>'ob_exec_id' IS NOT NULL", ")", "SELECT count(*)                                AS distinct_ext_ids,", "       sum(rows_per_id)                        AS total_entity_rows,", "       count(*) FILTER (WHERE rows_per_id > 1) AS ext_ids_with_multiple_rows,", "       max(rows_per_id)                        AS worst_case_rows_for_one_id", "FROM (SELECT ext_id, count(*) AS rows_per_id FROM p GROUP BY 1) g;", "", "-- Q4. Name ambiguity and anchor quality. Quantifies why name is not an identity (D3),", "--     and how much the employer anchor can be trusted for resolution and review.", "WITH p AS (", "  SELECT DISTINCT upper(btrim(mt.match_text))             AS name_key,", "                  e.id                                    AS entity_id,", "                  (e.original_id->'id'->>'value')::bigint  AS corp_id", "  FROM nvw_match.entities e", "  JOIN nvw_match.text_match_xref x ON x.entity_id = e.id AND x.active", "  JOIN nvw_match.master_text     mt ON mt.id = x.master_text_id", "  WHERE e.context->>'type' = 'person'", "    AND e.original_id->'id'->>'table' NOT LIKE 'ind_vw.%'", "    AND e.original_id->'id'->>'value' ~ '^[0-9]+$'   -- guard the ::bigint cast", ")", "SELECT count(*)                              AS distinct_names,", "       count(*) FILTER (WHERE corps > 1)     AS names_spanning_multiple_corps,", "       count(*) FILTER (WHERE entities > 1)  AS names_with_multiple_entity_rows,", "       max(corps)                            AS worst_corps_for_one_name,", "       count(*) FILTER (WHERE valid_corps = 0 AND corps > 0) AS names_whose_anchors_are_all_invalid", "FROM (", "  SELECT p.name_key,", "         count(DISTINCT p.corp_id)  AS corps,", "         count(DISTINCT p.entity_id) AS entities,", "         count(DISTINCT c.id)        AS valid_corps", "  FROM p LEFT JOIN cvw.corporations c ON c.id = p.corp_id", "  GROUP BY 1", ") g;", "```", "", "**ExecView side (run against the accelerate database, `xvw` schema).** These size the seed", "population now that Official Board cards are the primary source (D9).", "", "```sql", "-- Q5. The OB card population, and how duplicated it is on the OB person key.", "SELECT count(*)                                                          AS ob_cards,", "       count(DISTINCT pc.person_info->'OBEXEC'->>'VALUE')                AS distinct_ob_exec_ids,", "       count(*) FILTER (WHERE pc.person_info->'OBEXCS'->>'VALUE' IS NOT NULL) AS cards_listing_related_ids,", "       count(*) FILTER (WHERE pc.person_info->'OBNLWC'->>'VALUE' IS NOT NULL) AS cards_flagged_no_longer_with_company", "FROM xvw.people_cards pc", "WHERE pc.data_source_id = 20;   -- ExecView IS the Official Board feed; no source is", "                                -- literally named \"The Official Board\" (\u00a77.2)", "", "-- Q6. How many OB cards can already anchor an affiliation edge?", "SELECT count(*)                                                            AS ob_cards,", "       count(*) FILTER (WHERE pc.person_info->'OBCOMP'->>'VALUE' IS NOT NULL) AS with_ob_company,", "       count(*) FILTER (WHERE pc.person_info->'KPIOID'->>'VALUE' IS NOT NULL) AS with_polaris_id,", "       count(*) FILTER (WHERE pc.person_info->'OBHIRE'->>'VALUE' IS NOT NULL) AS with_hire_date", "FROM xvw.people_cards pc", "WHERE pc.data_source_id = 20;   -- ExecView IS the Official Board feed; no source is", "                                -- literally named \"The Official Board\" (\u00a77.2)", "```", "", "Also worth one line, since it settles a loose end: `SELECT count(*) FROM xvw.people;` \u2014 that table", "is FK-referenced only by 2023-era migrations and no current model, and is empty locally. If it holds", "prod rows, it is a person population this spec has not accounted for.", "", "**Results \u2014 measured 2026-08-18.** T0 is closed except for one follow-up (\u00a77.3).", "", "### 7.1 News side: the matchable person population", "", "| Measure | Value |", "|---|---|", "| Person entities in `nvw_match` | **22,389** |", "| Carrying `ob_exec_id` | 21,593 (96.4%) |", "| Distinct `ob_exec_id` values | **20,145** |", "| Rows collapsed by keying on `ob_exec_id` | 1,448 (6.7%); 1,316 ids have >1 row, worst case 6 |", "| Context keys present, in total | `type`, `job_title` (2,673 distinct), `ob_exec_id` \u2014 **nothing else** |", "", "Provenance mix:", "", "| `original_id.id.table` | Rows | With `ob_exec_id` |", "|---|---|---|", "| `off_brd.subsidiaries` | 19,110 (85%) | 19,110 (100%) |", "| `off_brd.id_match` | 2,483 (11%) | 2,483 (100%) |", "| `refinitiv.ceos` | 796 (3.6%) | **0** |", "", "Name ambiguity, over 16,344 distinct names: **1,066 names span multiple corps** (worst case 4) and", "1,185 names carry multiple entity rows.", "", "**What this settles:**", "", "- **D1 holds, with a measured payoff.** `ob_exec_id` covers 96.4% of the population and collapses", "  1,448 duplicate rows on load. The fallback path (master row id) is needed for exactly one", "  population \u2014 the 796 `refinitiv.ceos` rows, 3.6% \u2014 which is small enough to handle without a", "  dedicated mechanism.", "- **D3 holds, quantitatively.** Name-only identity would wrongly merge 1,066 names that span", "  different companies \u2014 and that is *within the officer population*, where names are relatively", "  well-behaved. It would be far worse across the tier-B population.", "- **No second vendor key exists on the news side.** Master-data person entities are Official", "  Board-derived only; there is no Prospeo id in `nvw_match`. Cross-source resolution happens on the", "  ExecView side, not here (\u00a77.2).", "- **85% of matchable people anchor to a subsidiary corp**, not a top-level one. Affiliation edges", "  will frequently target the subsidiary \u2014 which is the more precise answer, and the legal-hierarchy", "  edges already relate it to its parent.", "", "### 7.2 ExecView side: the seed population", "", "Card counts by source (`xvw.data_sources`; no source is literally named \"The Official Board\" \u2014", "**`ExecView` (id 20) is the OB feed and `Pegasus` (id 58) is Prospeo**, both `3RD PARTY` and", "**not** client-scoped):", "", "| Source | Cards | Distinct `OBEXEC` | `OBCOMP` | `KPIOID` | `OBHIRE` | `OBQUIT` |", "|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|", "| **ExecView (Official Board)** | **502,409** | **491,310** | 502,409 (100%) | **0** | 113,841 (22.7%) | 27,009 (5.4%) |", "| **Pegasus (Prospeo)** | 81,953 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |", "| LinkedIn | 10,854 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |", "| TransUnion submitted (`CLIENT`) | 3,619 | 0 | 0 | 3,619 (100%) | 0 | 0 |", "", "Roughly 90 further sources are `src_type = KADS` and client-scoped \u2014 per-client card sets, out of", "scope as a registry source.", "", "`xvw.people` is **empty**. The vestigial-table loose end is closed; there is no unaccounted", "population.", "", "**What this changes in the spec:**", "", "- **`OBEXCS` and `OBNLWC` are defined in the data dictionary but populated on zero cards.** D9", "  claimed `OBEXCS` showed ExecView already models one-human-many-ids; that is unsupported.", "  Deactivating an affiliation edge cannot key on `OBNLWC` \u2014 use `OBQUIT` (5.4% coverage) or", "  absence-on-refresh.", "- **`KPIOID` is absent on every OB card.** The hoped-for existing link into our corp id space does", "  not exist for this feed; only client-submitted cards carry it. Mapping `OBCOMP \u2192 cvw.corporations`", "  is its own resolution step in T5 \u2014 though note master data has already solved it for the", "  matchable subset, which is what `off_brd.subsidiaries` / `off_brd.id_match` are.", "- **`OBCOMP` is on 100% of OB cards**, so every seeded person has an employer to anchor on even", "  where dates are missing.", "- **OB and Prospeo share no key.** Pegasus cards carry no `OBEXEC`, so resolving a Prospeo person", "  against an OB person needs a matching pass on name + company + email/LinkedIn \u2014 the same shape as", "  the existing `client_people_matches` weighted match. That is real work in T3, not a lookup.", "", "### 7.3 Follow-up query \u2014 Prospeo's identity keys", "", "Prospeo's cards carry none of the OB fields, and we do not yet know what identity they *do* carry.", "Before T3 commits to a `source_system` design for Prospeo:", "", "```sql", "SELECT k AS person_info_key, count(*) AS cards_with_key", "FROM xvw.people_cards pc", "JOIN xvw.data_sources ds ON ds.id = pc.data_source_id", "CROSS JOIN LATERAL jsonb_object_keys(", "    CASE WHEN jsonb_typeof(pc.person_info) = 'object' THEN pc.person_info", "         ELSE '{}'::jsonb END", ") AS k                       -- guard inside the LATERAL: a WHERE predicate does not", "                             -- reliably run before a set-returning function", "WHERE upper(ds.src_name) = 'PEGASUS'", "GROUP BY 1", "ORDER BY 2 DESC;", "```", "", "### 7.4 Seed breadth \u2014 RESOLVED: seed the full Official Board population", "", "**Master data covers 4.1% of the people ExecView knows** (20,145 of 491,310). The two capabilities", "pull in opposite directions on that gap:", "", "- **Event linking needs matchability.** *Before T4*, a person links to an event only if their name", "  reaches `nvw_match.master_text` \u2014 true for the 20,145 and nobody else. *After T4*, registry-backed", "  candidate generation covers the whole active person registry, subject to D13's fail-closed", "  disambiguation; actual coverage is measured in shadow mode before enablement.", "- **The corp-hub people view needs coverage.** \"Show me the people we have for this company\" is", "  near-useless at 4%.", "", "**Decision (D12): seed the full OB population.** A registry person no article mentions is harmless \u2014", "it behaves exactly like a CVW corporation nobody writes about \u2014 and matchability can be grown", "afterwards with no re-seed, because canonical ids do not change.", "", "**One caveat on how this was argued.** An earlier draft justified D12 by saying the corp-hub people", "view \"is worthless at 4% coverage\". That reasoning does not hold: 4.1% is person matchability against", "*news master data*, which is a different quantity from the share of tracked companies that would show", "at least one person. Seeding does not by itself create edges either \u2014 those need T5's `OBCOMP`", "resolution. D12 stands on its own merits (breadth is cheap, ids are stable, matchability grows later),", "not on that number. The corp-hub coverage question is a real and separate measurement (\u00a712).", "", "**Licence: confirmed permitted** by the system owner, 2026-08-19.", "", "**Scale: confirmed as a blocker, not a caveat.** `ent.entities` holds ~1,960 rows today; the seed", "takes it past 493,000, making people 99.6% of the registry. The audit below found one real", "performance cliff and one correctness gap on the agent-facing path, so the mitigation ships", "**before** the seed runs (T8).", "", "### 7.5 Agent-facing entity queries \u2014 audited", "", "`common/agents/tools/resolve_entity.py` is the tool agents use to resolve a name to an entity.", "", "**Correctness gap \u2014 agents cannot see people at all, seeded or not.** Candidates are filtered by", "`entity_type.in_(_SUPPORTED_ENTITY_TYPES)`, which resolves to", "`SETUP_SUPPORTED_ENTITY_TYPES = (CVW, MVW, IVW, BVW, BRV)`", "(`common/agents/vocabulary/setup_projection.py:30`) \u2014 its comment reads \"PERSON and GVW are not", "supported in MVP\". A PVW row would be filtered out of every candidate list. Three further places", "need the same admission:", "", "| Site | Change |", "|---|---|", "| `common/agents/vocabulary/setup_projection.py:30` | Add `PVW` to `SETUP_SUPPORTED_ENTITY_TYPES` |", "| same file, `SETUP_ENTITY_TYPE_DESCRIPTIONS` | Add a PVW description \u2014 it feeds the prompt roster |", "| `common/models/enum/account_type.py:41` | Add `PVW` to `GloballyValidEntityTypes` (people are global, not client-scoped like MVW/IVW) |", "| `common/agents/tools/resolve_entity.py` | The tool description and the generated entity-type description are hard-coded text, not derived from the projection |", "| `common/agents/skills/strategy_setup_orchestrator/prompt.md` | Explicitly instructs the agent **not** to resolve a person. A projection that admits PVW while the prompt forbids it yields a tool the model will not call |", "| `signals/app/services/agent_drafts.py` `_validate_entity_id` | **Not covered by the above \u2014 it is the hole.** It accepts a directly-submitted UUID for any active entity whose type is in `GloballyValidEntityTypes`, and its docstring states it \"does NOT re-run the `resolve_entity` ILIKE search\". Adding PVW to that set therefore admits `PROVISIONAL` people to authored scope unless this path applies the tier rule itself |", "| `CoverageWarning.PERSON_RESOLUTION_DEFERRED` | Stop emitting it. The enum value may stay for historical artifacts |", "", "**Tier gating is two boundaries, not one.** Filtering `resolve_entity` handles the search path;", "`_validate_entity_id` handles the paste-a-UUID path. D14's guarantee that provisional people are", "event-linkable but not authorable is only true if both enforce it.", "", "A test already asserts that every `AccountType` **outside** `SETUP_SUPPORTED_ENTITY_TYPES` is absent", "from the prompt (`tests/common/agents/skills/test_strategy_setup_orchestrator.py:799`), so this is a", "coordinated projection + prompt + test change, not a one-line edit.", "", "**Performance cliff.** `resolve_entity` runs `display_name ILIKE 'x%'`, falls back to", "`ILIKE '%x%'` when the prefix returns nothing, and sorts `ORDER BY display_name, id` under a", "`LIMIT` of at most 25. **`ent.entities` has no index on `display_name`** \u2014 the model carries only", "the five typed partial-unique indexes plus `superseded_by`. At ~1,960 rows that is a trivial", "sequential scan. At ~493,000 it is a full scan plus a sort **on every agent-authoring call**, and", "the contains-fallback will fire more often once person names dominate the table.", "", "Mitigation, all precedented in this codebase:", "", "- **A GIN trigram index on `lower(display_name)`.** `pg_trgm` is already installed", "  (`CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pg_trgm`, 2023 workspaces migration) and already used with", "  `gin_trgm_ops` in the kads client-people search. A trigram index serves both the prefix and the", "  contains pattern.", "- **A minimum query length before the contains path.** Three characters is trigram's natural floor;", "  a one- or two-character contains match selects a huge slice of a 493k table and the `LIMIT`", "  cannot rescue the sort that precedes it.", "- **Create it `CONCURRENTLY`**, following Accelerate's own precedent \u2014 a non-transactional", "  migration issuing `op.execute` plus an invalid-index cleanup guard, as in the `doc_info` article-id", "  index migration. (Accelerate has no shared lock-safe DDL helper; that one is DataLake2's.)", "", "**Consumers to verify rather than assume** (all currently join by `entity_id` / PK, which is", "index-served, but the gate should prove it at scale): `intel_agents/app/cascade/layers/l1.py`,", "`intel_agents/app/agents/tools/get_entity_context.py`, `common/utils/entity_coalescing.py`,", "`signals/app/services/{signal,agent,intel,pattern}_read_service.py`,", "`common/services/intel/anchor_account.py`.", "", "### 7.6 Band sizing for person matching \u2014 the second follow-up measurement", "", "D13 routes each candidate into one of three bands, and the boundaries are configuration that must be", "**derived, not guessed**. This section measures the candidate side of that: how separable the seeded", "people are from each other, and how many of them have a real affiliation anchor available.", "", "**Be clear about what it cannot do.** It does not predict band rates, LLM call volume, latency or", "decline behaviour, because the deterministic score also reads article-side evidence \u2014 a stated title,", "a named employer, a co-occurring entity \u2014 that no registry query can model. Boundaries cannot be", "derived from this SQL alone. **The band rates come from running the scorer in shadow mode over a", "representative article sample**, which T4 owns and which must happen before production enablement.", "This measurement is the input that makes the shadow run interpretable, not a substitute for it.", "", "**Run after T3 and T5**, against **accelerate**. It reads the real registry under its own stored", "normalization, and it uses the actual affiliation edges rather than a master-data export \u2014 those edges", "are what T4 consumes, so measuring anything else measures the wrong thing.", "", "```sql", "-- Registry-side name collisions and the affiliation anchors actually available to T4.", "WITH seeded AS (", "    SELECT p.id              AS person_id,", "           p.normalized_name,", "           e.id              AS entity_id", "    FROM pvw.persons p", "    JOIN ent.entities e", "      ON e.entity_type = 'PVW'", "     AND e.person_id   = p.id", "     AND e.is_active", "    WHERE p.normalization_version = :current_normalization_version", "      AND p.normalized_name <> ''", "), person_rows AS (", "    -- one row per person, so a person with several active source ids is not counted twice", "    SELECT s.person_id,", "           s.normalized_name,", "           count(DISTINCT r.target_entity_id) AS employer_count", "    FROM seeded s", "    LEFT JOIN ent.entity_relationships r", "      ON r.source_entity_id     = s.entity_id", "     AND r.relationship_family  = 'AFFILIATION'", "     AND r.target_entity_type IN ('CVW', 'BVW')", "     AND r.is_active", "    GROUP BY 1, 2", "), by_name AS (", "    SELECT normalized_name,", "           count(*)                     AS persons,", "           bool_and(employer_count > 0) AS every_person_has_employer", "    FROM person_rows", "    GROUP BY 1", "), name_shared_employers AS (", "    -- names where two colliding people share an employer: the anchor cannot", "    -- separate them, and nothing else in this data can either", "    SELECT s.normalized_name", "    FROM seeded s", "    JOIN ent.entity_relationships r", "      ON r.source_entity_id     = s.entity_id", "     AND r.relationship_family  = 'AFFILIATION'", "     AND r.is_active", "    GROUP BY s.normalized_name, r.target_entity_id", "    HAVING count(DISTINCT s.person_id) > 1", ")", "SELECT (SELECT count(*) FROM person_rows)                            AS registry_persons,", "       count(*)                                                      AS distinct_names,", "       count(*) FILTER (WHERE persons = 1)                           AS unique_names,", "       coalesce(sum(persons) FILTER (WHERE persons > 1), 0)          AS shared_name_persons,", "       count(*) FILTER (WHERE NOT every_person_has_employer)         AS names_with_an_unanchored_person,", "       coalesce(sum(persons) FILTER (", "           WHERE persons > 1", "             AND every_person_has_employer", "             AND normalized_name NOT IN (SELECT normalized_name FROM name_shared_employers)", "       ), 0)                                                         AS collisions_employer_separates,", "       max(persons)                                                  AS worst_name_collision", "FROM by_name;", "```", "", "**How to read it.**", "", "| Column | What it tells you |", "|---|---|", "| `unique_names` | People reachable on a name alone. Under D13 these are gray-zone inputs, not automatic matches, so this sizes **adjudicator volume**, not match volume |", "| `collisions_employer_separates` | Whether the employer anchor is a real discriminator. Two same-named people at *different* companies are separable; the ones excluded by `name_shared_employers` are same name at the same company, and no signal in this data separates them |", "| `names_with_an_unanchored_person` | Where `OBCOMP` resolution failed (T5), so the anchor does not exist even though the person does. A large number here means T5's target resolution, not D13, is the thing to fix |", "| `shared_name_persons` | The upper bound on ambiguity. Every one of these is a decline unless the article supplies a title or co-occurrence |", "", "**Also worth running once T5 lands**, since it answers \u00a712's corp-hub question directly rather than", "by inference: `active CVW entities with at least one active resolvable affiliation / all active CVW", "entities`, with the median and p10 people per covered company alongside it.", "", "", "## 8. Child tickets", "", "**One epic plus eight stories, T1\u2013T8.** T0 is closed evidence, listed for provenance and not filed.", "The two ratified scope additions \u2014 the evidence-promotion lane (D2) and affiliation edges (D6) \u2014", "account for T6 and T5. IDs assigned at filing.", "", "| # | Title | Repo | Type | Depends on | Phase |", "|---|---|---|---|---|---|", "| T0 | Measure the master-data person population \u2014 **closed, results in \u00a77** | \u2014 | Spike | \u2014 | done |", "| T1 | `PVW` entity type + `pvw.persons` + `pvw.person_source_ids` \u2014 **keystone** | Accelerate | Story | \u2014 | 1 |", "| T2 | Person context capture + person candidate observations | DataLake2 | Story | \u2014 (parallel now) | 0 |", "| T3 | Seed and reconcile persons from Official Board | Accelerate | Story | T1, **T8** | 2 |", "| T4 | **Person linking end to end: match, disambiguate, stamp, emit** | DataLake2 | Story | T1, T2, T3, T5 | 4 |", "| T5 | Affiliation edge family + officer/board seed | Accelerate | Story | T1, T3 | 3 |", "| T6 | Provisional minting + promotion lane for unknown people | Accelerate + DataLake2 feed | Story | T1, T2, T4 | 5 |", "| T7 | Admit `PVW` on every agent-facing path + PRD errata | Accelerate | Story | T1 | 2 |", "| T8 | Entity-resolution scale gate \u2014 **blocks the T3 seed** | Accelerate | Story | T1 | 2 |", "", "**T4 absorbs what earlier drafts split as T9.** The split assumed stamping already-matchable people", "was the cheap half and registry matching was an additive follow-up. It is not: the `matched_entities`", "rail is closed to registry-only people (\u00a76), so the \"cheap\" half could only ever have served 4% of", "the registry, and the follow-up would have had to build the real rail anyway. One ticket owns the", "rail, the disambiguation and the emit. There is no T9.", "", "**Natural split if this should be two epics:** T0\u2013T4 + T7 + T8 deliver the watchable-person", "capability (a user can point an agent at a person and get their events). T5\u2013T6 deliver the", "relationship graph and the coverage lane \u2014 though note T4 now depends on T5 for the affiliation", "anchor, so the split is no longer clean and the second epic would have to ship T5 first.", "", "### T0 \u2014 Measure the master-data person population (spike) \u2014 **CLOSED, do not file**", "", "Run 2026-08-18/19. Results are in \u00a77.1 and \u00a77.2 and are what D12, D13 and D14 were decided on. It is", "listed here so the epic records where its evidence came from; **there is nothing left to do and no", "ticket to raise.** Two follow-up measurements remain, and neither is this spike: Prospeo's identity", "keys (\u00a77.3, not blocking \u2014 T3 is Official Board only) and band sizing for person matching (\u00a77.6,", "needed before T4 is estimated, and it cannot run until T1 and T3 have).", "", "### T1 \u2014 `PVW` entity type + person tables \u2014 keystone (Accelerate)", "", "**Blocks:** T3, T4, T5, T6, T7.", "**Scope:** \u00a75.1\u2013\u00a75.2 \u2014 `pvw` schema; `pvw.persons` (internal integer PK, `display_name`,", "`admission_tier`, admission provenance, **no name uniqueness**); `pvw.person_source_ids` with", "`UNIQUE(source_system, source_id)` and an FK to `pvw.persons`; `PVW` added to `AccountType` and the", "friendly-name maps; `ent.entities.person_id` typed FK; `entities_typed_fk_chk` PVW arm; PVW partial", "unique index; UUIDv5 derivation; INSERT/UPDATE triggers; idempotent backfill; the", "`AccountType.PVW \u2192 PlatformEntity.person_id` entry in `_backing_column`.", "**The CHECK is rebuilt, not extended.** `entities_typed_fk_chk` is a single constraint over all typed", "FK arms, so adding PVW means dropping and recreating it with all six arms present. Worth saying because", "\"extend the CHECK with the PVW arm\" reads like an `ALTER` that does not exist.", "", "**Two resolvers, not one.** The existing `resolve_platform_entity_id(PVW, person_id)` takes a backing", "id. T4 does not have one \u2014 it has a vendor key from the article. So T1 also exports a **batch", "source-key resolver** taking `(source_system, source_id)` pairs and returning terminal survivor entity", "ids, in one set-based query, skipping inactive source rows. Without it T4 has no way to get from an", "`ob_exec_id` on a match to a PVW entity, and would invent a per-row lookup.", "", "**Also name explicitly:** the `PERSON_VIEW_SCHEMA` setting; model and module exports for the two new", "tables; both friendly-name maps (`AccountTypeNames` and `FriendlyAccountTypes`); and the", "`ALTER TYPE acc.account_type ADD VALUE 'PVW'` as its own predecessor migration, per the BVW/BRV", "precedent \u2014 a new enum value cannot be added and used in the same transaction.", "", "**Follows:** the BVW/BRV precedent. No new pattern is invented except the source-id table, which", "mirrors `nvw_match.entities_source_map`.", "**AC sketch:** inserting a `pvw.persons` row materializes exactly one `ent.entities` PVW row with", "the expected UUIDv5; rerunning the backfill is a no-op; the CHECK rejects a PVW row with any other", "typed FK set and a non-PVW row with `person_id` set; two persons may share a `display_name`; two", "`source_system` rows may point at one person; the same `(source_system, source_id)` cannot point at", "two people; `resolve_platform_entity_id(PVW, person_id)` returns the canonical id; a PVW entity can", "be superseded via the existing merge primitive with reason `DEDUP`; CVW/MVW/IVW/BVW/BRV behaviour", "unchanged.", "", "### T2 \u2014 Person context capture + person candidate observations (DataLake2) \u00b7 start now", "", "**Why now:** additive DataLake2-only storage, no platform dependency, cannot affect the matching", "trunk \u2014 the same reasoning that made org context capture the parallel-startable piece. It is also", "what feeds the promotion lane in T6.", "**Scope:**", "- Add `people.context` JSONB (nullable, fail-safe NULL) carrying the D4 per-article fields, assembled", "  the same way `organizations.context` is.", "- **Publish the contract, and share a base.** Add `entity_classification/schemas/person_context.py`", "  as a peer of `org_context.py` \u2014 Pydantic, `extra=\"forbid\"`, documented null/empty semantics and", "  documented identity keys, so writer and readers cannot drift. Extract `ArticleContextBase`", "  (`article_geography`, `industries`, `co_occurring_entities`) and have both `OrgContext` and", "  `PersonContext` inherit it. Lift the envelope computation into one shared helper:", "  `assemble_and_write_org_context` already reads the article's organization, person and location rows", "  in one pass and already computes the article-level dimensions once, so this names an existing seam", "  rather than adding a layer. Refactoring `OrgContext` onto the base changes no stored data \u2014 the", "  column is JSONB and `jsonb` does not preserve object-key order.", "- **Extend the extraction payload \u2014 the prerequisite D4 names.** Add optional `title_or_role`,", "  `employer_name` and `aliases` to `common/schemas/entities/people.py`, in the same", "  `XxxAttr(value, evidence)` shape `OrgTypeAttr` already uses for organizations and whose docstring", "  invites exactly this. `ExtractedEntity` is `extra=\"ignore\"`, so payloads without the fields keep", "  parsing. Without this, D13's deterministic score has no title feature at all and every person falls", "  into the gray zone.", "- **Carry the new fields all the way through \u2014 extending the schema alone does nothing.**", "  `merge_people_payload` builds each merged person as a three-key literal", "  (`{\"is_owner\": ..., \"evidence\": [], \"confidence\": None}`), so anything else on the payload is", "  silently dropped at that step and never reaches `people` or its context. The merge must aggregate", "  the new fields too, and the aggregation rule has to be stated because it is not obvious: **union the", "  aliases; keep every distinct stated title and employer rather than picking one.** Collapsing them to", "  a single value would erase precisely the disagreement D13 declines on.", "- **Keep `merge_people_payload`'s normalized-name collapse.** One row per name per article, the same", "  as `organizations`, whose `uq_ec_orgs_article_name` has the identical shape. D3's grouping operates", "  on the rollup *across* articles \u2014 one article contributes one sighting with one anchor \u2014 so the", "  within-article collapse does not defeat it. Two same-named subjects in one article is as rare here", "  as it is for companies; where it happens, D13 declines on the inconsistent evidence rather than", "  guessing (D13). Do **not** re-key the table on a mention ordinal.", "- **`anchor` is two first-class nullable columns, not a blob key:** `anchor_type` and `anchor_value`,", "  with `anchor_type` following D3's precedence \u2014 corp id, then employer name, then geography, then", "  none. A rollup cannot group on something that only exists inside JSON. Derive each person's anchor", "  from *that person's* `employer_name` once organizations resolve, upgrading it to a uniquely resolved", "  corp id where possible \u2014 not from the article's undifferentiated organization list.", "- New `candidate_person_observations` table plus a `candidate_person_rollup` view, written for each", "  persisted `people` row that D13 did not link, carrying the cross-article aggregates from D4.", "  The observation key is `(article_id, normalized_name, layer_one_activity_id)` with", "  `NULLS NOT DISTINCT` \u2014 the activity id alone is a scope, not a key. **The anchor is deliberately not", "  in the key.** It is derived from organizations that may resolve on one attempt and not the next, so", "  keying on it would make a retry insert a second row instead of upserting the first. The anchor is", "  mutable payload, refreshed on upsert; the rollup groups on its current value, which is what D3 asks", "  for.", "- **`distinct_publishers` needs a defined publisher identity.** Derive `publisher_key` as the", "  normalized registrable domain from the article's source URL using the existing publisher-hostname", "  helper; NULL when there is no source URL. `distinct_publishers` counts distinct non-NULL values, so", "  a corpus with missing URLs cannot inflate the count that D14's evidence bar reads.", "- **Carry status and provenance:** an observation-group status and the `promoted_person_id` it minted,", "  with explicit rollup precedence so a durable rejection (T6) cannot be buried by later observations.", "- **Separate table, not a widened `candidate_observations`.** That table's `organization_id` is NOT", "  NULL and its `type_hint` is the `org_type` enum; relaxing either would weaken a live contract the", "  SoS feed reads. Share the normalization, upsert and rollup-precedence *code*, not the table.", "- Document the surface in `.docs/codebase/` alongside the candidate rollup contract, stating that a", "  rollup row is not a person.", "**AC sketch:** person context persisted on new rows and validated through `PersonContext`, NULL on", "historical rows and on the fail-safe path; `OrgContext` output is unchanged by the base refactor", "(compared as parsed JSON, not as text); an extraction payload omitting the new person fields still", "parses and yields a valid `PersonContext`; a person's anchor is derived from their own `employer_name`", "rather than the article's organization list; unlinked people produce", "candidate rows; retry upserts the same activity row and never resets status or `promoted_person_id`;", "replay inserts new rows and advances `last_seen`; rollup groups on `(normalized_name, anchor_type,", "anchor_value)`; `distinct_publishers` counts registrable domains and ignores NULLs; a rejected group", "stays rejected after re-observation; no change to matching behaviour, `doc_entity_map`, or the", "business candidate surface.", "", "### T3 \u2014 Seed and reconcile persons from Official Board (Accelerate)", "", "**Depends on:** T1 (target schema), **T8 (the seed must not run before the scale gate is in place \u2014", "D12)**. T0 is closed (\u00a77).", "", "**Official Board only.** Prospeo/Pegasus is **out of this ticket** until \u00a77.3 has measured what", "identity its cards actually carry. Pegasus cards carry no `OBEXEC` and no other OB field (\u00a77.2), and", "email, LinkedIn URL or name must not be silently promoted to a `source_id` \u2014 that would bake a", "non-identity into `UNIQUE(source_system, source_id)`. Adding Prospeo later is a `source_system` value", "and a loader, not a migration (D1).", "**Primary source: the Official Board population reachable through ExecView** (D9) \u2014 `OBEXEC` as the", "external key, `OBEXCS` as the same-human hint. `nvw_match` person entities resolve against the same", "id space via `context.ob_exec_id` rather than being read as a second master. Prospeo and any future", "source are configuration plus a `source_system` value, not a rewrite.", "**Scope:** idempotent loader over the complete OB card snapshot, read in bounded batches and", "resolved with **set-based prefetch and upsert \u2014 no per-card SELECT**. 491k records through a", "per-record lookup loop is the N+1 this sentence exists to prevent. Resolution order: active", "`(OFFICIAL_BOARD, OBEXEC)`; then any id listed in `OBEXCS` where populated (measured at zero today,", "\u00a77.2, so this is a forward-compatibility path and not the primary one); then the documented", "conservative name-plus-company-plus-title rule. Writes the source-id rows, refreshes `display_name`,", "sets `admission_tier = VERIFIED`. Takes identity and affiliation fields only \u2014 contact PII stays in", "ExecView.", "", "**Duplicate reconciliation is deterministic, not best-effort.** Where two persons already exist for", "one human, pick the survivor by `VERIFIED` over non-`VERIFIED`, then earliest `admitted_on`, then", "lowest person id; reparent the victim's source-id rows; merge the victim's PVW entity with reason", "`DEDUP`; preserve the survivor's original admission provenance. Two runs must choose the same", "survivor.", "", "**A person with no resolvable employer is still a person.** Missing or unmappable `OBCOMP` does not", "reject the record and never mints a corporation; it is reported for T5.", "**Coordinate with the ExecView owners** on read access and on whether the loader reads cards or the", "upstream OB feed directly.", "**AC sketch:** a rerun on unchanged input creates no new person and no new source-id row (it may", "still refresh `display_name` and last-seen, so \"no-op\" is stated as \"no new identity rows\", not \"no", "writes\"); one external id resolves to exactly one person; two source ids for one human can be", "attached without creating a second person; every seeded person has exactly one `ent.entities` PVW row;", "canonical ids do not change between runs; two runs over the same duplicate pair choose the same", "survivor; a record whose employer does not resolve is still admitted and is counted in the", "unresolved-employer report; the loader issues a number of queries proportional to batches, not to", "records; the run reports counts by `source_system`, by admission tier, and by merge.", "", "### T4 \u2014 Person linking end to end: match, disambiguate, stamp, emit (DataLake2)", "", "**Depends on:** T1 (the type), T2 (context capture supplies the scoring signals), T3 (registry", "populated), T5 (affiliation edges supply the co-occurrence anchor).", "**Why it is one ticket.** Absorbs what earlier drafts split as T4 + T9. The split assumed the", "`matched_entities` rail could carry person links and that registry matching was additive; it cannot,", "so a split would build the rail twice and the first half would deliver 4% coverage. See \u00a76.", "", "**This ticket is deliberately prescriptive.** The design choices below are settled, not options \u2014", "each one has a failure mode that is expensive to unwind after the fact.", "", "**Where the id goes.** `entity_classification.people.platform_entity_id` (new nullable UUID column).", "**Not** `matched_entities.platform_entity_id`: its `master_text_id` and `nvw_entity_id` are `NOT NULL`", "and a registry-resolved person has neither. Follow the `entity_classification.locations` precedent,", "which already carries `platform_entity_id` on its own row with no `matched_entity_id` at all. Do not", "relax `matched_entities` nullability \u2014 that unique constraint is a live contract the organization", "path depends on.", "", "**Person-originated `matched_entities` rows stay NULL-stamped** and keep producing the existing CVW", "`Person: {name}` / `Entity CEO: {name}` attribution in `doc_entity_map`, unchanged. A person now", "*additionally* carries a PVW canonical id on their `people` row. The two are separate on purpose.", "", "**Two passes, in this order.** The current pipeline matches people at step 2 and organizations at", "step 3 (`entity_classification.py`), so at person-matching time no employer is resolved and D13's", "corroborating signals do not exist yet. Therefore:", "", "1. **Pass 1 \u2014 collect, choose nobody.** Gather candidate registry people from both sources: the", "   existing `nvw_match` path, and `pvw.persons` by normalized name. Stamp nothing.", "2. **Then** organizations, locations and industries match and `people.context` is assembled (T2).", "3. **Pass 2 \u2014 one decision per person.** Collapse candidates sharing a verified source id, score the", "   remainder, and apply D13's bands once over the combined candidate set. Stamp at most one PVW id", "   per `people` row.", "", "**Both person paths go through that one decision.** The existing `nvw_match` path does not keep its", "own behaviour \u2014 it contributes candidates and nothing more. A same-name `nvw_match` hit must not", "produce a PVW stamp that bypasses D13, or the epic ships the over-attribution default it explicitly", "inverted.", "", "**The adjudication call sits outside the transaction window.** Phase A holds a Datalake write session", "plus master and Accelerate read sessions open across steps 1\u20136b. Per this project's critical", "invariant a transaction never stays open across external I/O, so the gray-zone LLM call must run", "after those sessions commit \u2014 structured like the existing step-7 sync I/O. Do not open the LLM call", "inside Phase A.", "", "**Batch reads only, and bounded.** One set-based query for registry candidates and one for", "affiliations. No query per extracted person and none per candidate \u2014 fetching from a 491k-row table in", "a loop over an article's people is the N+1 this line exists to prevent.", "", "**Candidate retrieval has a hard cap, and overflow fails closed.** The candidate set is the union of", "source-key-resolved `nvw_match` candidates, exact matches on the stored normalization, and a bounded", "variant search for the alias cases. A very common name can exceed any sane cap, and **truncating", "silently would hand the adjudicator an arbitrary subset and call the result a decision.** On overflow,", "produce no link and record the observation with the fact that the candidate set was too large to", "adjudicate \u2014 a recorded, countable outcome, distinct from a confident non-match.", "", "**Also in scope:**", "- Add `\"PVW\"` to `_ENTITY_TYPE_TO_PROVENANCE_KEY` in `event_extraction/services/extraction_service.py`,", "  keyed to `person_ids` (not `person_match_ids` \u2014 a registry-only person has no match row).", "- Build the `P1..Pn` alias group in `build_known_entity_refs` from `people` rows with a non-NULL", "  `platform_entity_id`. Remove the blanket person exclusion and its docstring; the NULL-`platform_entity_id`", "  filter stays and now does the work.", "- Teach the extraction prompt that person entities exist and may hold `subject` / `agent` roles.", "- Widen the ESS bridged-type set in `event_synthesis/services/entity_display_names.py:90` and fix its", "  stale docstring. **BVW and BRV are also missing from that set** \u2014 latent today because nothing emits", "  them, so it is folded in here. The fix must not admit an unbridged type (`GVW`, \u00a712).", "- **Add `platform_entity_id: str | None = None` to `org_context.PersonRef`**, and select", "  `Person.platform_entity_id` directly when building person refs \u2014 the existing `MatchedEntity` join", "  stays for `matched_entity_id` provenance and does not supply this. The docstring currently says the", "  key \"must be absent (not null) for a person ref\", and the writer carries the paired comment \"Persons", "  are never stamped with a `platform_entity_id` \u2014 no MatchedEntity join\"; both go. Defaulting the field", "  keeps pre-PVW payloads valid under `extra=\"forbid\"`, so no version field is needed. Prove it with", "  contract tests: a pre-PVW payload still validates, and an existing `OrgContext` payload is", "  dict-equal apart from the added person-ref key.", "", "**The document and enqueue gate \u2014 the reason a person-only article works at all.** Today", "`sync.py:211` returns `None` when there are no `doc_entity_map` reasons, and `entity_classification.py`", "enqueues Event Extraction only inside `if doc_id:`. Reasons are corp-, market- or industry-keyed", "(`build_doc_entity_reasons`: \"People/Orgs => corp-level (CVW), corp_id = pio_id\"), so an article whose", "only match is an unaffiliated person produces no reason, no document, and no event extraction \u2014 which", "is precisely the population \u00a71.4 says this epic exists for.", "", "**A person stamped with a PVW id is sufficient to create or recover the document and enqueue Event", "Extraction, with no `doc_entity_map` row written.** Attribution is untouched; only the gate changes.", "Two things must be checked rather than assumed, and they are acceptance criteria:", "", "- `render_article_pdf(article, reasons)` is called with the reason list (`sync.py:630`). Confirm it", "  produces a correct PDF when that list is empty, or give the person-only path a defined alternative.", "- Confirm no consumer of `doc.doc_entity_map` assumes a document has at least one row. If one does,", "  that finding escalates \u2014 it would force the person-keyed-attribution decision this epic defers.", "", "**Gate:** does not enable in production before the merge-health check exists (\u00a711).", "", "**AC sketch:** a person resolved only through the registry (no `master_text` row) reaches", "`raw_events.entities_involved` with `entity_type=\"PVW\"` and a `person_ids` provenance array, and", "reaches `source_event_entities`; a person resolved through `nvw_match` reaches the same places by the", "same code path; within one successful attempt a gray-zone person produces at most one adjudication request, and a", "retry with the same request fingerprint reuses a persisted terminal verdict where one exists rather", "than re-calling; an adjudicator failure or timeout produces no link and one recorded observation;", "**an article whose only match is a person produces a document, an enqueued Event Extraction message", "and zero `doc_entity_map` rows**; the PDF path is exercised with an empty reason list; a confident non-match", "produces no link and one recorded observation carrying its candidate set; no person link is ever", "produced without passing D13's decision; the adjudicator is not called while any DB session is open", "(asserted, not assumed); registry candidate lookup issues a bounded number of queries independent of", "the number of people in the article; person-originated `matched_entities` rows remain NULL-stamped", "and `doc_entity_map` output is byte-identical; BVW/BRV no longer log `entity_type_not_bridged`;", "existing CVW/MVW/IVW refs, aliases and drop counters unchanged; organization, location and industry", "matching unchanged.", "### T5 \u2014 Affiliation edge family + officer/board seed (Accelerate)", "", "**Depends on:** T1, T3 (needs persons to attach to).", "**Scope:** \u00a75.4 \u2014 the `AFFILIATION` family with `OFFICER_OF` / `BOARD_MEMBER_OF` / `EMPLOYED_BY`;", "endpoint CHECK `PVW \u2192 CVW|BVW`; **explicitly excluded from the closure walk**; nullable", "`effective_from` / `effective_to` with their ordering CHECK; and an idempotent seed from the Official", "Board card fields (D9) \u2014 `OBCOMP` for the employer, `OBPACO` / `OBULCO` for ownership context,", "`OBHIRE` / `OBQUIT` for time bounds where present, and **`TITLE` as the edge's role title** \u2014 the", "registry-side input to D13's title feature, which has no other source for most seeded people. Fallback where a card is absent:", "`off_brd.subsidiaries` (85% of the matchable population, \u00a77.1), `off_brd.id_match`, `refinitiv.ceos`,", "with the role from `nvw_match.entities_context.job_title`. Written with `managed_by_seed = TRUE`.", "", "The family name and all three kind values are **new PostgreSQL enum values and need migrations** \u2014", "they are not application-level strings.", "", "**Target resolution and refresh semantics are in \u00a75.4** and are part of this ticket, not left to", "implementation: `OBCOMP` has no bridge into our corp id space, an unresolved target means no edge", "rather than a minted corporation, and deactivation-by-absence is permitted only after a complete", "source read.", "", "**`OBBOSS` is out of scope.** A reporting line needs its own relationship kind, and \"if a reporting", "edge is wanted\" is not implementable scope. Add it deliberately or not at all.", "", "**AC sketch:** an affiliation edge can be written between a person and a corp or business, and is", "rejected between two organizations or two people; an edge with both dates NULL is valid and active;", "an edge with `effective_to` earlier than `effective_from` is rejected; a reverse lookup by target", "entity returns that company's people with their role kind in one indexed query; the ownership closure", "output is byte-identical before and after affiliation edges exist (the regression that proves closure", "exclusion); the seed is idempotent and never deactivates a producer-written edge; a **partial or", "failed** source read deactivates nothing; a person whose `OBCOMP` resolves to no tracked company is", "retained with no edge and is counted; a person who changes employer ends with the prior managed edge", "inactive and the new one active; deactivating an affiliation edge leaves historical event tags", "untouched.", "", "### T6 \u2014 Provisional minting + promotion lane for unknown people (Accelerate + DataLake2 feed)", "", "**Depends on:** T1 (target), T2 (the evidence), **T4** (the linking path a minted person attaches", "to, and the `people` row the stamp is written onto). Production enablement follows T4.", "**Scope:** the tier-B route from D2/D14, in two halves.", "", "*Minting (automatic).* An eligibility rule over the person rollup \u2014 distinct articles, distinct", "non-NULL publishers, time span, stable `(normalized_name, anchor_type, anchor_value)`, confidence", "floor \u2014 mints a `pvw.persons` row with `admission_tier = PROVISIONAL`, which materializes an", "`ent.entities` PVW row through the T1 trigger. Minting never fires when D13 declines against people", "we already have \u2014 a confident non-match or a gray-zone decline is a fail-closed drop, not a new", "person (D14).", "", "**Minting is forward-only.** The person is linked to the article that crossed the bar and to every", "article after it. Sightings recorded before the bar stay as candidate evidence and are **not**", "retroactively linked to their events. An earlier draft promised that backfill; it is not", "implementable from what we store. `candidate_person_observations.article_id` records that the person", "appeared somewhere in an article \u2014 not which raw event, and not their role in it \u2014 and event", "extraction never saw a person reference for those articles at all, so there is nothing to attach to.", "Linking the person to every event in each prior article would assert involvement the article never", "supported, which is exactly what D13 fails closed to avoid. Recovering those links would require an", "event-extraction replay, which is out of scope for this epic and out of line with its forward-only", "posture. The visible consequence, stated so nobody meets it as a surprise: a person admitted on six", "sightings starts with one event, and their history looks thinner than the evidence that admitted them.", "", "**Minting is exactly-once, via a durable claim.** Eligibility is evaluated repeatedly, so the mint", "needs an atomic conflict key rather than a check-then-insert. Claim it with a `person_source_ids` row", "\u2014 `source_system = 'DATALAKE_PROVISIONAL'`, `source_id` a versioned fingerprint of the candidate group", "\u2014 so the source-id primary key makes a concurrent or repeated evaluation recover the existing person", "instead of minting a second one. Do not derive a fresh person id on every evaluation.", "", "**Where the mint sits in the pipeline, and why it cannot float.** The threshold-crossing article is", "the first one that links (forward-only, above), and T4 makes a stamped person sufficient to create the", "document and enqueue Event Extraction. So the mint and the stamp must complete **before** that gate is", "evaluated \u2014 after the article's people, context and observations are written, and before the step-7", "sync and step-8 enqueue. Run it later and the person is unstamped when the gate is read, so the very", "article that admitted them does not link, and forward-only quietly becomes forward-only-from-the-next-one.", "", "**The mint and the stamp are in different databases, so state the order.** The evidence lives in", "DataLake2, the person is minted in Accelerate, and the stamp lands back on a DataLake2 `people` row \u2014", "with no distributed transaction available and the standing rule that no transaction stays open across", "external I/O. The sequence is therefore: read the evidence and **close** the DataLake read scope; make", "the atomic claim and mint in Accelerate and commit; then open a **fresh** DataLake write scope to stamp", "`people.platform_entity_id`. A crash between the mint and the stamp must be recoverable \u2014 the claim row", "is the durable record, so the next pass over the same candidate group recovers the existing person and", "completes the stamp rather than minting again or losing the link.", "", "*Promotion (reviewed).* A review surface lists provisional people with their evidence; a reviewer", "promotes (tier flip to `EVIDENCE_PROMOTED`, which makes them resolvable in agent authoring),", "rejects, or merges into an existing person via the merge primitive. Promotion changes no ids and", "rewrites no event links.", "", "**Rejection has to be durable.** Rejecting sets `ent.entities.is_active = false` **and** records a", "durable rejected status on the candidate group, so later observations of the same name cannot mint it", "again. Without the second half, a rejected non-person re-crosses the bar and returns. The surface", "should distinguish \"not a person\" from \"duplicate of someone we have\" \u2014 they lead to different", "actions.", "", "**No automatic expiry.** A provisional person who is never promoted is a hidden, evidence-bearing", "audit record, not a leak: it is tier-gated out of agent authoring (T7) and costs a row. Report", "provisional age and count as operational metrics instead, and revisit if the count misbehaves.", "", "**Calibrate before shipping thresholds:** run the rule over existing rollup data and inspect what it", "would have minted. Do not ship guessed numbers.", "**Build it type-agnostic.** The same machinery should serve business candidates later (D14); avoid", "person-only assumptions in the eligibility and promotion paths.", "**Open:** who staffs review (\u00a712.7).", "**AC sketch:** a person crossing the bar gets exactly one `pvw.persons` row and one `ent.entities`", "PVW row, and a repeated or concurrent eligibility evaluation recovers that same person rather than", "minting a second; **the threshold-crossing article itself links** \u2014 the stamp lands before the", "document/enqueue gate is evaluated; a crash between the mint and the stamp is recovered on the next", "pass through the claim row, with no second person and no lost link; the threshold-crossing article links, and articles after it link, while sightings", "recorded before the bar produce no event links; a provisional person links to events but does **not**", "appear in `resolve_entity` candidates and is rejected on direct-UUID scope submission; promotion is a", "tier flip with no id change and no re-linking; a rejected group stays rejected after re-observation of", "the same name; merge-into-existing causes merge-aware readers to resolve prior references to the", "survivor (it does not rewrite tag rows \u2014 see D5); a case where D13 declined against known people never", "mints; the rule's parameters are configuration, not constants.", "", "### T7 \u2014 Admit `PVW` on every agent-facing path + PRD errata (Accelerate)", "", "**Depends on:** T1 (and D7). **Pairs with T8** \u2014 admission without the index is a performance", "regression; the index without admission is dead weight.", "**Scope:** the four admission sites found in \u00a77.5 \u2014 `SETUP_SUPPORTED_ENTITY_TYPES` and", "`SETUP_ENTITY_TYPE_DESCRIPTIONS` (`common/agents/vocabulary/setup_projection.py:30`),", "`GloballyValidEntityTypes` (`common/models/enum/account_type.py:41`), and the scope validation in", "`signals/app/services/agent_drafts.py:2027` that reads it \u2014 plus Signal Engine scope/routing/", "surfacing accepting `PVW` in `primary_entities[]` / `secondary_entities[]` and `signal_entities`;", "the resolver stops emitting the people-centric capability warning. Update the prompt roster and the", "paired test at `tests/common/agents/skills/test_strategy_setup_orchestrator.py:799`, which asserts", "that every type outside the supported tuple is absent from the prompt. PRD v1.9 errata for \u00a73.4,", "the Layer 1 \"PERSON/PVW entities are not routed\" line, and the assumption list, plus the", "corrections in \u00a72.1.", "**Two admission sites \u00a77.5 missed**, both hard-coded text rather than data: `resolve_entity`'s own", "tool description and its generated entity-type description, and", "`common/agents/skills/strategy_setup_orchestrator/prompt.md`, which explicitly instructs the agent", "not to resolve a person \u2014 **and the strategy-*edit* path's roster too, not only initial setup; an", "agent that can be created with a person but not edited to add one is a worse bug than neither.** A projection that admits PVW while the prompt forbids it produces a tool", "the model will not call. Also stop emitting the `PERSON_RESOLUTION_DEFERRED` coverage warning; the", "enum value may stay for historical artifacts.", "", "**Tier gating, enforced in two places \u2014 not one.** `resolve_entity` must offer only verified and", "evidence-promoted people. That alone is not a boundary: `agent_drafts._validate_entity_id` accepts a", "directly-submitted UUID for any active entity whose type is in `GloballyValidEntityTypes`, and its", "docstring states it \"does NOT re-run the `resolve_entity` ILIKE search\". Since this ticket adds PVW to", "that set, a provisional person's UUID pasted straight into a scope would be accepted and D14's", "guarantee would be false. Both paths must join through `person_id` and admit only `VERIFIED` or", "`EVIDENCE_PROMOTED`. Runtime event linking does not apply this filter \u2014 provisional people still link", "to events (D14).", "**AC sketch:** `resolve_entity` returns person candidates for a person name; a provisional person is", "never offered as a candidate **and is rejected when its UUID is submitted directly to scope", "validation**; the setup prompt no longer forbids resolving a person; an agent can scope to", "a person entity and receives signals routed on it; people are treated as globally valid (not", "client-scoped like MVW/IVW); the prompt roster lists PVW and the projection test passes; person", "entities are subject to the same skip-on-missing-canonical discipline as every other type; the PRD", "no longer describes a three-type registry or an `xvw_id` column.", "", "### T8 \u2014 Entity-resolution scale gate (Accelerate) \u00b7 **blocks the T3 seed**", "", "**Why it exists:** the seed takes `ent.entities` from ~1,960 rows to ~493,000 and", "`common/agents/tools/resolve_entity.py` has no `display_name` index while falling back to a", "leading-wildcard `ILIKE` under an `ORDER BY \u2026 LIMIT` (\u00a77.5). Landing the seed first would degrade", "every agent-authoring call.", "**Scope:**", "- **A GIN trigram index whose expression matches the live query.** The query is", "  `PlatformEntity.display_name.ilike(pattern)` \u2014 plain `display_name ILIKE $1`. An index on", "  `lower(display_name)` would **not** be used for it, because an expression index only serves a query", "  that contains the same expression. Pick one and make them agree: index `display_name` directly with", "  `gin_trgm_ops` and keep the `ILIKE`, or change the query to `lower(display_name) LIKE lower(:pattern)`", "  and keep the expression index. `gin_trgm_ops` supports both `~~` (LIKE) and `~~*` (ILIKE), so either", "  pairing works \u2014 an unmatched pairing ships an index the planner ignores, which is worse than no", "  index because it reads as mitigated. Create it `CONCURRENTLY` following Accelerate's precedent: a", "  non-transactional migration using `op.execute` with an invalid-index cleanup guard. Accelerate has", "  no shared lock-safe DDL helper \u2014 that one lives in DataLake2 and must not be cited here.", "  `pg_trgm` is already installed and already used with `gin_trgm_ops` in the kads client-people search.", "- **A minimum query length on both paths, not just the fallback.** Three characters is trigram's", "  natural floor. Guarding only the contains-fallback still lets a one- or two-character *prefix* scan", "  a large slice of a 493k table and sort it under the `LIMIT`.", "- Benchmark `resolve_entity` at production-like scale \u2014 seed a scratch environment to ~493k person", "  rows \u2014 for prefix hit, contains fallback, and short-query cases.", "- Audit, at that scale, the other `ent.entities` consumers listed in \u00a77.5. They join by", "  `entity_id` / PK today, so they should be fine; the gate is to prove it, not assume it.", "**AC sketch:** `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` shows the trigram index is used for both the prefix and", "the contains path at ~493k rows \u2014 this is the assertion that catches an index/query mismatch, and it", "is not satisfied by a latency number alone; resolver p95 and p99 are measured on the same instance", "before and after loading the person rows, with the acceptable ratio and the absolute", "ceiling **agreed, written into the ticket, and attributed to a named approving role before the", "benchmark runs** \u2014 \"within an agreed bound\" is not an acceptance criterion until the bound exists", "(this spec sets no number \u2014 see \u00a712); one- and two-character", "queries are rejected before either lookup; **entity-type-filtered** resolution results are unchanged", "(same members, same order) \u2014 untyped results are expected to include people and are therefore not", "required to match; the index is created without blocking writes; the short-query floor is", "configuration, not a constant; every consumer in the \u00a77.5 list has a measured result recorded in the", "ticket.", "", "## 9. Sequencing", "", "```", "Phase 0 \u2014 start now, no dependencies", "  T2 Person context capture + person candidates      (DataLake2, additive)", "     \u2514\u2500 its schema work can start immediately; its producer behaviour is", "        specified in T2 and should not be inferred", "", "Phase 1 \u2014 keystone", "  T1 PVW type + pvw.persons + pvw.person_source_ids  (Accelerate)", "", "Phase 2 \u2014 after T1, parallel", "  T7 Admit PVW on agent-facing paths + PRD errata", "  T8 Entity-resolution scale gate                    (index + guard + benchmark)", "", "Phase 2b \u2014 after T8 (never before)", "  T3 Seed + reconcile from Official Board            (~491k persons)", "", "Phase 3 \u2014 after T3 (needs persons to attach to)", "  T5 Affiliation edges + officer/board seed          (Accelerate)", "", "Phase 4 \u2014 after T2 + T3 + T5", "  T4 Person linking end to end                       (DataLake2; the whole ~491k)", "     \u2514\u2500 production enablement also waits on the \u00a711 merge-health gate", "", "Phase 5 \u2014 after T4", "  T6 Provisional minting + promotion lane            (calibrate on real rollup data first)", "```", "", "**Why T8 gates T3.** The seed is the event that makes the table large. Running it before the index", "and the short-query guard exist degrades every agent-authoring call, and a 493k-row table is a bad", "place to discover that. T7 and T8 pair: admission without the index is a regression, the index", "without admission is dead weight.", "", "**Why T4 moved to Phase 4.** Earlier drafts put stamping in Phase 3 and registry matching in Phase 4,", "on the assumption they were separable. They are not (\u00a76, \u00a78): one rail serves both, and building it", "needs T2's context for the scoring signals and T5's edges for the co-occurrence anchor. So T4 sits", "after all three of its inputs rather than ahead of two of them.", "", "**Why T6 is last.** It now depends on T4 as well as T1 and T2 \u2014 a provisional person is only useful", "once there is a linking path to attach them to, and the mint writes onto the same `people` row T4", "stamps. Its thresholds also need rollup data that only exists once T2 has been running, and its review", "surface is worth building after the verified path has proven the schema.", "", "**One external gate.** T4 should not land before a merge-health check exists (\u00a711).", "", "## 10. Cross-repo and cross-team map", "", "- **Accelerate platform:** T1 (keystone \u2014 schemas, enum, triggers, backfill, resolver), T3 (seed +", "  resolution), T5 (affiliation edges), T6 (promotion lane), T7 (Signal Engine + PRD), T8 (scale", "  gate). The `AccountType` enum is shared with account types, so T1 needs the platform owner's", "  sign-off on the enum value even though D7 creates no accounts.", "- **DataLake2:** T2 (context + candidates + the shared context contract), T4 (match, disambiguate,", "  stamp, emit, ESS bridged set), T6 feed side. T4 is the one ticket that adds an LLM call to the L1", "  path, so its transaction boundary needs a second pair of eyes at review.", "- **Signal Engine / PRD owner:** T7, plus the \u00a72.1 errata.", "- **Master-data owner:** the Prospeo/Official Board source mix behind a", "  future Prospeo loader, and the", "  long-term question of whether the person population is maintained well enough to be a registry", "  source.", "- **Review owner (open, \u00a712.7):** whoever staffs the T6 promotion queue.", "- **No SoS dependency.** Unlike the BVW tier, nothing here waits on the SoS project. The provisional", "  tier's promotion path is T6, staffed internally; the open dependency is who owns that review queue", "  (\u00a712.7), not an external verifier.", "", "---", "", "## 11. Interaction with event matching (DAT-8299) \u2014 not a driver", "", "This spec is a capability, not a bug fix. DAT-8299 (event matching under-merges) is a separate,", "actively-investigated defect whose cause is being narrowed in scoring and retrieval. Nothing here", "changes candidate retrieval, scoring, or matching logic. Two interactions are worth recording so", "neither ticket surprises the other.", "", "**A side benefit.** For a story whose subject is a person, the entity set today holds whatever", "organisations each article happened to name \u2014 incidental, and unstable between articles. Once the", "person is an entity, the entity-overlap retrieval channel has a seed that is actually about the", "story. That is a precision improvement to one of three retrieval channels, not a fix: DAT-8299's", "own analysis shows clusters that already shared an entity, a type and a date and still failed to", "merge, so the defect it is chasing lives elsewhere.", "", "**A risk to manage.** Adding person entities changes the entity sets the overlap factor is", "computed over, and it can cut both ways \u2014 it helps when both sides name the person, and hurts", "when one article names them and the other does not, because the union grows while the", "intersection does not. So: **T4 should not land before a merge-health check exists** (DAT-8299", "requirement 4), and that check should be read before and after. Sequence T4 with that ticket's", "owner.", "", "---", "", "## 12. Open items and risks", "", "1. **Prospeo's identity keys are still unmeasured.** The news side is settled \u2014 the only context", "   keys on person entities are `type`, `job_title` and `ob_exec_id` (\u00a77.1) \u2014 but Pegasus cards carry", "   none of the OB fields and we do not yet know what identity they *do* carry. \u00a77.3 holds the query.", "   The identity model survives any answer (that is the point of owning our own id). **T3 is scoped to", "   Official Board only** so this does not block filing; adding Prospeo later is a `source_system`", "   value and a loader, not a migration. What must not happen is promoting an email, a LinkedIn URL or", "   a name to `source_id` to get Prospeo in sooner \u2014 that bakes a non-identity into a uniqueness", "   constraint.", "2. **Verified-source quality is not ours to control.** If a source is noisy, the registry inherits", "   the noise. Mitigations: D5 (audited merge), and the option to admit only the subset carrying an", "   external id. T0's numbers are in (\u00a77.1): the OB population is 96.4% covered by `ob_exec_id`, so", "   the id-bearing-subset option is available if quality turns out to be a problem.", "3. **Two sets of thresholds are unset by design, and neither should be guessed.** T6's promotion bar", "   calibrates against real rollup data \u2014 set too low, the registry fills with one-off names; too high,", "   and the celebrity/politician population stays unwatchable, which is the thing tier B exists to fix.", "   D13's band boundaries calibrate against \u00a77.6 plus a shadow-mode run. Both are configuration, and", "   the spec deliberately states no starting values. An outside review asked for the numbers to be", "   fixed before filing; that is declined on the grounds that a guessed threshold is harder to", "   dislodge than an empty one.", "4. **T8's latency bound is also unset, deliberately.** \"Within an agreed bound of the current p95\"", "   needs the bound agreed and written into the ticket before the benchmark runs. The reviewer offered", "   concrete figures; those are a product call, not a reviewer's, so none are recorded here.", "5. **Person data is more sensitive than company data.** `pvw.persons` holds a name, an admission", "   tier and external ids \u2014 no contact details, and nothing from the client contact subsystem (D8,", "   D9). Any later proposal to enrich person rows should re-open that question rather than inherit", "   this decision. A promoted person is a Polaris assertion about a named human, which is a higher", "   bar than a vendor-sourced officer record.", "6. **Affiliation edges will tempt a closure change.** Once the edges exist, \"why doesn't watching", "   Amazon catch a Bezos event?\" is a reasonable question with a wrong easy answer. The right answer", "   is opt-in scope expansion at agent-authoring time (D6), not closure. Record it in the T5 ticket", "   so it survives the first request.", "7. **Review staffing for T6 is unassigned.** The businesses path has SoS as an external verifier;", "   people have no equivalent, so promotion review is internal. Who owns that queue, and at what", "   volume it stops being viable, is an open call.", "8. **RESOLVED \u2014 `PVW` code, `pvw` schema.** The question looked like one decision; it is two, with", "   very different stakes, and separating them settles it (D11).", "", "9. **RESOLVED \u2014 seed the full OB population (D12).** Licence confirmed permitted. Scale is handled", "   as a hard gate: T8 ships the trigram index, the short-query guard and a measured benchmark", "   **before** T3 runs the seed (\u00a77.5).", "10. **Residual scale risk beyond the resolver.** T8 audits the other `ent.entities` consumers at", "    scale, but they are only measured, not redesigned. If one of them turns out to scan, that is a", "    finding for T8 to escalate rather than absorb quietly.", "11. **RESOLVED \u2014 matching covers the whole registry (D13, T4).** Registry-backed matching with", "    banded scoring and gray-zone adjudication closes the ~471k gap. What to watch as it lands: the", "    confident-non-match rate, because people fail closed and a high rate means real coverage loss;", "    the gray-zone share, because it sets adjudicator cost; and adjudicator agreement, because a", "    verdict nobody checks is a threshold nobody set. Name variants \u2014 \"Bob Iger\" against \"Robert A.", "    Iger\" \u2014 are no longer an open risk: they are what the gray-zone adjudicator exists to resolve,", "    with D4's recorded variants as its evidence.", "12. **RESOLVED \u2014 the invariant relaxation is approved** by the org-epic owner (2026-08-19). The", "    residual item is the follow-up it implies: business candidates have the identical gap (an SMB", "    seen fifty times still cannot attach to one event) and the T6 machinery is built type-agnostic", "    to serve them. Extending it is not in this epic's scope and needs its own ticket against the org", "    epic.", "13. **`GVW` is still enum-only.** Out of scope, but the same bridge-plus-allowlist gap applies, and", "   the ESS allowlist fix in T4 must not accidentally admit an unbridged type.", "14. **T4 puts an LLM call on the L1 article path for the first time.** D13's gray-zone adjudication is", "   the first external model call in entity classification. The transaction-scoping constraint is", "   stated in D13 and restated in T4, but it is the highest-consequence thing in the epic to get", "   wrong: Phase A holds three sessions open, and a call inside that window holds locks across the", "   network. Cost and latency per article are also new surface \u2014 the gray-zone share from \u00a77.6 is what", "   sizes them.", "15. **Corp-hub coverage is unmeasured, and no surface ships until it is.** \u00a73 now says this epic", "   delivers the data and the query, not the view. Measure after T5 as `active CVW entities with at", "   least one active resolvable affiliation / all active CVW entities`, plus median and p10 people per", "   covered company (\u00a77.6). A corp-hub people view is enabled only once its product owner ratifies an", "   acceptable floor against that number \u2014 a view that opens empty for most companies is worse than no", "   view. This gates the surface, not the registry or the relationship graph, and it does not block", "   filing.", "16. **The `PersonRef` contract change has readers we have not enumerated.** Adding", "   `platform_entity_id` to `org_context.PersonRef` touches a contract declared `extra=\"forbid\"` (D4).", "   Defaulting the field to `None` keeps old payloads valid, and review found no production reader of", "   DataLake `organizations.context` \u2014 but \"none found\" is not \"none exists\", so T4 lists the consumers", "   before the change lands rather than discovering one through a validation error.", "17. **A document with no `doc_entity_map` rows is a new state.** T4 lets a stamped person create or", "   recover a document without a reason (\u00a73). Two things must be confirmed there, not assumed: that the", "   PDF render behaves with an empty reason list, and that nothing downstream requires a document to", "   have at least one row. If something does, that forces the person-keyed-attribution decision this", "   epic deliberately defers, and it becomes an escalation rather than something T4 absorbs.", "18. **Person-keyed article attribution is deferred, deliberately.** `doc.doc_entity_map` has a", "   three-arm CHECK and typed `corp_id` / `market_id` / `industry_id` columns; admitting people means a", "   new column, a new arm, a new index, and every consumer of that table beginning to see PVW rows.", "   Nothing in this epic needs it \u2014 event linking runs through `source_event_entities`, which is a", "   different table answering a different question. Worth taking on its own merits later.", "", "---", "", "## Appendix A \u2014 verification log", "", "Every claim checked against source or a live database on 2026-08-18.", "", "| Claim | Verdict | Source |", "|---|---|---|", "| Person matches are never stamped with `platform_entity_id` | **CONFIRMED** | `entity_classification/services/helpers/people_funcs.py:93-106` |", "| Person matches are excluded from the extraction prompt, and unstamped rows are filtered before it is built | **CONFIRMED** | `event_extraction/services/helpers/prompt_context.py:86-108` |", "| `entities_involved` provenance-key map admits CVW/MVW/IVW only | **CONFIRMED** | `event_extraction/services/extraction_service.py:480-484` |", "| ESS drops any entity type outside `{CVW, MVW, IVW}` with `entity_type_not_bridged` | **CONFIRMED** \u2014 stale for BVW/BRV, but latent: nothing emits those codes today | `event_synthesis/services/entity_display_names.py:90` |", "| `AccountType` = CVW, MVW, GVW, IVW, BVW, BRV | **CONFIRMED** | `accelerate_models/common/models/enum/account_type.py`; `enum_range(NULL::acc.account_type)` |", "| `ent.entities` bridges five types via typed FKs + CHECK + partial unique indexes | **CONFIRMED** | `accelerate_models/common/models/entities.py` |", "| Live rows exist for BVW and BRV | **CONFIRMED** (32 each, local dev) | `select entity_type, count(*) from ent.entities group by 1` |", "| `bvw.businesses` / `brv.brands` are `(id, name UNIQUE)` stubs with externally minted ids | **CONFIRMED** | `accounts/app/models/{business_view/businesses,brand_view/brands}.py` |", "| Merge/supersede shipped with `DEDUP` reason | **CONFIRMED** | `common/models/entity_merge_history.py`, `enum/merge_reason.py`; `ent.entity_merge_history` exists |", "| `ent.entity_relationships` shipped; families LEGAL_HIERARCHY / BRAND_OPERATION / ASSOCIATIVE; endpoints CVW/BVW/BRV only | **CONFIRMED** | `common/models/entity_relationships.py` |", "| `source_event_entities.entity_id` is an untyped FK to `ent.entities.id` | **CONFIRMED** \u2014 no schema change needed for PVW | `event_synthesis/app/models/source_event_entities.py` |", "| `resolve_platform_entity_id` is a `_backing_column` map; the DataLake2 wrapper is type-agnostic | **CONFIRMED** | `common/db/operations/entities.py`; `entity_classification/services/helpers/platform_entity_resolution.py` |", "| Person kind is decided by `nvw_match.entities.context.type == 'person'` | **CONFIRMED** | `entity_classification/services/helpers/nvw_match_parsing.py:212-240` |", "| `ob_exec_id` is parsed from person context and used nowhere | **CONFIRMED** | `nvw_match_parsing.py:118,138`; only other references are a schema field and its docstring |", "| `nvw_match.entities_context` exposes `ob_exec_id` and `job_title` as columns | **CONFIRMED** | `microservices/master_db_models/nvw_match/entities_context.py` |", "| Person provenance tables are officer/board/CEO sources | **CONFIRMED** for `off_brd.id_match`, `refinitiv.ceos`; population mix unmeasured (T0 Q1) | `.docs/codebase/ENTITY_MATCHING.md` provenance table |", "| `people` has no `context` column; `organizations` does | **CONFIRMED** | `entity_classification/models/{people,organizations}.py` |", "| Candidate observation store is organizations-only (`organization_id` NOT NULL, `org_type` type hint) | **CONFIRMED** | `entity_classification/models/candidate_observations.py` |", "| Business rollup dedupes on `normalized_name` alone and accepts over-merge | **CONFIRMED** | `.docs/codebase/CANDIDATE_ROLLUP_CONTRACT.md` |", "| Unmatched people persist as `people` rows with `matched_entity_id = NULL` and no candidate row | **CONFIRMED** | `people_funcs.py` (Person row written regardless of matches) |", "| `KADS_SCHEMA=xvw`; the `kads` code module maps onto the physical `xvw` schema | **CONFIRMED** | `accelerate/.env:68`, `.env.template:102`; `pg_namespace` lists `xvw`, no `kads` |", "| `xvw` people tables are client/contact-scoped, not a public-figure master | **CONFIRMED** | `kads/app/models/{cards,execs,exec_card_matches,card_sources}.py`; `common/meta/person_info.py` |", "| No `pvw` schema exists | **CONFIRMED** | local `pg_namespace` |", "| PRD PVW paragraph unchanged from v1.8 to v1.9 | **CONFIRMED** | `accelerate/.docs/prds/signal-engine-v1.9.md:215,223,368,529,979` |", "| ExecView Official Board cards carry `OBEXEC`, `OBEXCS`, `OBCOMP`, `OBPACO`, `OBULCO`, `OBHIRE`, `OBQUIT`, `OBNLWC`, `OBBOSS`, `PIOIDS`, `KPIOID` | **CONFIRMED** | `kads/app/utils/constants.py:46-66` |", "| Card visibility is client-entitled via `xvw.linked_sources` | **CONFIRMED** | `kads/app/api/v1/sample_data/execs/get_linked_sources.py`; `kads/app/utils/profile_match/query/query_match_weighted.py` |", "| No `xvw.data_sources` row is literally named \"The Official Board\" \u2014 the OB feed is `ExecView` (id 20) | **CONFIRMED** \u2014 an earlier row here claimed the opposite; \u00a77.2 is authoritative | \u00a77.2 measurement |", "| `xvw.people_cards` is one row per (person, data source) \u2014 cannot be an `ent.entities` FK target without duplicating entities | **CONFIRMED** | `kads/app/models/cards.py` (`data_source_id` FK); `OBEXCS` field |", "| ExecView is an active production service, not a legacy namespace | **CONFIRMED** by the system owner in review | \u2014 |", "| Canonical ids derive from `(entity_type, backing_id)` only \u2014 the schema name is not an input | **CONFIRMED** | `common/constants/platform_entities.py:19`; `alembic/versions/\u2026dat_6603_create_ent_entities_bridge_.py` |", "| Accelerate runs one alembic chain across all schemas (no per-service cadence) | **CONFIRMED** | single `alembic.ini` + `alembic/versions/` \u2014 362 migrations, `xvw` 44 / `ent` 15 |", "| Which vendor id spaces exist on person entities, their coverage, and the duplication rate | **MEASURED 2026-08-18** \u2014 only `type`, `job_title`, `ob_exec_id`; 96.4% coverage; 1,448 rows collapse on the id | \u00a77.1 |", "| Row counts and dedupe state of the OB card population | **MEASURED 2026-08-18** \u2014 502,409 cards, 491,310 distinct `OBEXEC`; `OBEXCS` / `OBNLWC` / `KPIOID` on zero | \u00a77.2 |", "| What identity Prospeo/Pegasus cards carry | **UNMEASURED** \u2014 T3 is scoped to Official Board so this does not block filing | \u00a77.3 |", "| Registry-side name-collision structure and employer-anchor reach | **UNMEASURED** \u2014 needs T1/T3 to have run | \u00a77.6 |", "", "**Verified during external PRD review, 2026-08-20.** Each of these changed a design decision.", "", "| Claim | Verdict | Source |", "|---|---|---|", "| `matched_entities.master_text_id` and `nvw_entity_id` are both `NOT NULL`, so a registry-only person cannot be represented there | **CONFIRMED** | `entity_classification/models/matched_entities.py` |", "| `entity_classification.locations` carries `platform_entity_id` on its own row and has no `matched_entity_id` \u2014 the precedent people follow | **CONFIRMED** | `entity_classification/models/locations.py` |", "| L1 matches people at step 2 and organizations at step 3, so no employer anchor exists at person-matching time | **CONFIRMED** | `entity_classification/services/entity_classification.py:191` (people), `:196` (orgs) |", "| Phase A holds a Datalake write session plus master and Accelerate read sessions open across steps 1\u20136b, committing before step-7 sync I/O | **CONFIRMED** | same file, Phase A comment |", "| `merge_people_payload` merges to one entry per normalized name, collapsing same-named people before any anchor exists | **CONFIRMED** | `entity_classification/services/helpers/people_funcs.py:186` |", "| `resolve_entity` queries `display_name ILIKE :pattern`, so a GIN index on `lower(display_name)` would not be used | **CONFIRMED** | `common/agents/tools/resolve_entity.py:81`; `gin_trgm_ops` includes `~~` and `~~*` per `contrib/pg_trgm/pg_trgm--1.3.sql` |", "| `agent_drafts._validate_entity_id` admits any active entity in `GloballyValidEntityTypes` and \"does NOT re-run the `resolve_entity` ILIKE search\" | **CONFIRMED** | `signals/app/services/agent_drafts.py` |", "| `merge_entities` never rewrites `source_event_entities` / `signal_entities` / `pattern_entities`; readers resolve via `resolve_terminal_survivor` | **CONFIRMED** | `common/db/operations/entities.py` docstring |", "| `org_context.OrgContext` is a published Pydantic contract with `extra=\"forbid\"`; `PersonRef` deliberately omits `platform_entity_id` | **CONFIRMED** | `entity_classification/schemas/org_context.py` |", "| `assemble_and_write_org_context` already computes the article-level dimensions once and excludes self per row | **CONFIRMED** | `entity_classification/services/helpers/entity_helpers.py:682` |", "| `jsonb` does not preserve object-key order, so refactoring `OrgContext` onto a base changes no stored data | **CONFIRMED** | PostgreSQL docs, JSON Types: \"`jsonb` does not preserve white space, does not preserve the order of object keys, and does not keep duplicate object keys\" |", "| Banded scoring with LLM gray-zone adjudication is an established pattern here, not a new mechanism | **CONFIRMED** | `event_synthesis/services/scoring/composite.py:81-91`; `web_extraction/services/helpers/borderline_verifier.py`; UNI-18333 |", "| `gpt-5.6-luna` is already an available chat model | **CONFIRMED** | `ChatModel.GPT_5_6_LUNA` |", "", "**Verified during external PRD review round 2, 2026-08-25.** Each changed a design decision.", "", "| Claim | Verdict | Source |", "|---|---|---|", "| The L1 extraction payload for a person carries only `name`, `evidence`, `confidence`, `is_owner` \u2014 no title, employer or aliases | **CONFIRMED** | `common/schemas/entities/people.py`; `common/schemas/entities/base_entities.py` |", "| Organizations already receive a per-entity extracted attribute, and the codebase names the extension shape | **CONFIRMED** | `common/schemas/entities/organizations.py` \u2014 `OrgTypeAttr`, docstring: \"Future typed attributes follow the same `XxxAttr(value, evidence)` shape\" |", "| `entity_classification.organizations` is name-keyed per article, exactly like `people` \u2014 the within-article collision limit is shared, not person-specific | **CONFIRMED** | `uq_ec_orgs_article_name` vs `uq_ec_people_article_name` |", "| A document is created only when at least one `doc_entity_map` reason exists, and Event Extraction is enqueued only when a document exists | **CONFIRMED** | `services/helpers/external/sync.py:211`, `:624`; `services/entity_classification.py` `if doc_id:` |", "| Person reasons are corp-keyed, so an unaffiliated person produces no reason | **CONFIRMED** | `accelerate_table_writes.py:1208` `build_doc_entity_reasons` \u2014 \"People/Orgs => corp-level (CVW), corp_id = pio_id\" |", "| The PDF render consumes the reason list | **CONFIRMED** | `sync.py:630` `render_article_pdf(article, reasons)` |", "| `doc.doc_entity_map` admits only CVW / MVW / IVW, via a three-arm CHECK over typed id columns | **CONFIRMED** | `accelerate/documents/app/models/doc_entity_map.py` |", "| \u00a75.1 as previously written lacked `normalized_name` and source-row `is_active`, which \u00a77.6's query referenced | **CONFIRMED** \u2014 both added to \u00a75.1 and T1 | this spec |", "", "**Verified during external PRD review round 3, 2026-08-26.**", "", "| Claim | Verdict | Source |", "|---|---|---|", "| `merge_people_payload` builds each merged person as a three-key literal, so any new payload field is dropped before it reaches `people` | **CONFIRMED** | `people_funcs.py:186` \u2014 `{\"is_owner\": False, \"evidence\": [], \"confidence\": None}` |", "| The registry holds no job title for a seeded person; `nvw_match.entities_context.job_title` covers only the already-matchable subset, and OB cards carry `TITLE` | **CONFIRMED** \u2014 hence T5 carries `TITLE` onto the affiliation edge | `kads/app/utils/constants.py`; \u00a75.1; \u00a77.1 |", "| Accelerate has no shared lock-safe DDL helper \u2014 `CONCURRENTLY` is issued via `op.execute` in a non-transactional migration with a hand-written invalid-index guard | **CONFIRMED** \u2014 an earlier draft cited DataLake2's helper for an Accelerate migration | `accelerate/alembic/versions/\u2026dat_7984_doc_info_article_id_index.py` |", "", "## Appendix B \u2014 corrections to prior documents", "", "Recorded so the next reader does not re-derive from a stale premise.", "", "1. **People-entities planning handoff, fact 1** \u2014 `AccountType` has six values, five", "   bridged, not three.", "2. **People-entities planning handoff, fact 6** \u2014 the PVW blueprint is no longer the first", "   X-VW extension; BVW and BRV shipped ahead of it.", "3. **People-entities planning handoff, fact 7** \u2014 `kads` and `xvw` are the same tables:", "   `kads` is the code module, `xvw` is the physical schema (`KADS_SCHEMA=xvw`). The substantive", "   point stands and is stronger than stated: cards are per-data-source, frequently", "   client-licensed, contact-detail-bearing, and not deduplicated.", "4. **Entity Registry Expansion epic design (DAT-7349), \u00a74A** \u2014 \"no X-VW extension has been", "   implemented yet\" is now historical.", "5. **`accelerate/.docs/prds/signal-engine-v1.9.md` \u00a73.4** \u2014 three-type registry, absent merge", "   history, and the `xvw_id` / `data_source_id` person premise are all stale (\u00a75.3).", "6. **`event_synthesis/services/entity_display_names.py:36`** \u2014 docstring claims `ent.entities`", "   bridges CVW/MVW/IVW only; the allowlist consequently drops BVW and BRV. Latent \u2014 nothing emits", "   those codes today. Fix in T4.", "7. **`entity_classification/schemas/industry_references.py:66`** \u2014 `ob_exec_id` is documented as", "   an \"Execution or run identifier\". It is the officer/board provider's executive person id.", "8. **This spec's own first draft** proposed keying person identity on `ob_exec_id`, deferring both", "   the promotion lane and affiliation edges, and it described `xvw` as client-scoped contact data.", "   All four were corrected in review: identity is Polaris-owned with vendor ids demoted to", "   resolution keys (D1), unverified people get an evidence-and-review route in (D2), affiliation", "   edges ship in this epic (D6), and ExecView is an **active production service** whose separation", "   from the registry rests on differing jobs and data classes, not on it being legacy (D9). Note", "   that parts of `xvw` are not client-scoped at all: `people`, `people_cards` and `data_sources`", "   carry no `client_id`.", "9. **The PRD path moved** \u2014 the Signal Engine PRD now lives at", "   `accelerate/.docs/prds/signal-engine-v1.9.md`. Stale v1.8 PRD", "   pointers in the two plan documents were repointed.", "10. **This spec's own pre-review draft** made five design assumptions that external review", "   disproved. All are now verified in Appendix A, and each changed a decision: person links would", "   ride `matched_entities` (they cannot \u2014 its key columns are `NOT NULL`, so `people` carries the id", "   instead, following the `locations` precedent); D13's employer anchor would be available when", "   people are matched (it is not \u2014 organizations match one step later, hence T4's two passes); T8's", "   `lower(display_name)` index would serve the resolver (it would not \u2014 the query has no `lower()`);", "   tier-gating `resolve_entity` alone would keep provisional people out of authored scope (it would", "   not \u2014 `_validate_entity_id` accepts a UUID directly); and pre-mint sightings could be", "   retroactively linked to their events (they cannot \u2014 the candidate store records the article, not", "   the event or the role). It also split person linking across two tickets on the assumption the", "   first was cheap; T4 and T9 are now one story.", "11. **This spec's round-1 revision over-corrected on one point.** Round 1 flagged that", "   `merge_people_payload` collapses same-normalized-name mentions, and the revision accepted \"persist", "   them separately when anchors differ\". That was wrong twice over: D3's `(normalized_name, anchor)`", "   grouping operates on the rollup *across* articles, so a within-article collapse does not defeat it;", "   and `organizations` is name-keyed per article in exactly the same way, so the limit is shared rather", "   than person-specific. The collapse stays. What was genuinely missing was different \u2014 the extraction", "   payload carries no per-person title, employer or aliases at all (D4), which is an additive change", "   following the `OrgTypeAttr` precedent, not a re-keying of the table.", "12. **This spec's round-2 revision left four gaps that round 3 caught**, all recorded in Appendix A or", "   fixed in place: extending the extraction schema without carrying the fields through", "   `merge_people_payload`, which drops them; a title feature with no registry-side title for ~471k", "   people; an observation retry key containing a derived, mutable anchor, which would make a retry", "   insert rather than upsert; and a provisional mint with no stated position in the pipeline, which", "   would have left the threshold-crossing article unlinked. It also cited DataLake2's lock-safe DDL", "   helper for an Accelerate migration, and claimed a cross-environment UUID stability that", "   sequence-allocated backing ids cannot provide."], "blocks": [{"start": 1, "end": 13, "label": "SPEC \u2014 People as platform entities (PVW)"}, {"start": 14, "end": 63, "label": "0. The answer, up front"}, {"start": 64, "end": 108, "label": "1. The capability gap"}, {"start": 109, "end": 151, "label": "2. Current state \u2014 what changed since the last write-up"}, {"start": 152, "end": 198, "label": "3. Goals and non-goals"}, {"start": 199, "end": 776, "label": "4. Decisions"}, {"start": 777, "end": 889, "label": "5. Registry shape"}, {"start": 890, "end": 936, "label": "6. End-to-end flow after this lands"}, {"start": 937, "end": 1304, "label": "7. Measurement gate (T0)"}, {"start": 1305, "end": 1784, "label": "8. Child tickets"}, {"start": 1785, "end": 1830, "label": "9. Sequencing"}, {"start": 1831, "end": 1851, "label": "10. Cross-repo and cross-team map"}, {"start": 1852, "end": 1874, "label": "11. Interaction with event matching (DAT-8299) \u2014 not a driver"}, {"start": 1875, "end": 1964, "label": "12. Open items and risks"}, {"start": 1965, "end": 2045, "label": "Appendix A \u2014 verification log"}, {"start": 2046, "end": 2104, "label": "Appendix B \u2014 corrections to prior documents"}], "lineCount": 2104, "sha256": "f0fbaf6c1aa9f525b06dc2e91fb76a7fc8245bbbd606b1b5f0b9cadd023a79b7", "endsWithNewline": true});
